1
00:02:46,966 --> 00:02:50,605
Give me. Take these ones.

2
00:02:59,806 --> 00:03:01,765
Who is that?

3
00:03:08,486 --> 00:03:09,645
Come on, sisters.

4
00:03:09,806 --> 00:03:11,245
Come on, brothers.

5
00:03:11,606 --> 00:03:14,005
We have to finish this. Work harder.

6
00:03:14,166 --> 00:03:15,245
Come on.

7
00:03:16,446 --> 00:03:17,685
Come on, faster.

8
00:03:17,886 --> 00:03:20,005
Come on, come on.

9
00:03:20,286 --> 00:03:21,605
May your work be easy.

10
00:03:21,806 --> 00:03:24,605
Mother, how can we finish all this?

11
00:03:25,326 --> 00:03:27,485
We have to, dear. Come on.

12
00:03:31,366 --> 00:03:32,885
Come on, faster.

13
00:03:35,806 --> 00:03:37,285
Look at that.

14
00:03:37,486 --> 00:03:40,845
Mother, which soldier can that bread even feed?

15
00:03:44,246 --> 00:03:46,605
Even Ghazi won't be full with that.

16
00:03:48,766 --> 00:03:52,365
Whoever tries hard will find the success, dear.

17
00:03:52,606 --> 00:03:56,965
Our alps are going on a raid.
Who knows when they will be back?

18
00:03:57,606 --> 00:04:00,285
So we have to work much more.

19
00:04:04,126 --> 00:04:05,405
Come on.

20
00:04:06,886 --> 00:04:12,685
Every bread we bake and every meal
we cook will make our soldiers stronger!

21
00:04:27,686 --> 00:04:31,565
Bala Hatun, I'm ready to conquer with the alps!

22
00:04:32,206 --> 00:04:34,485
I know that, my boy.

23
00:04:34,606 --> 00:04:38,205
But we need you here in
the tribe for now, alright?

24
00:04:40,046 --> 00:04:43,405
Just let us know when you need, Bala Hatun.

25
00:04:45,806 --> 00:04:47,645
Bogac Alp! Bogac Alp!

26
00:04:48,406 --> 00:04:51,165
Bogac Alp, hurry up.
-Let's go.

27
00:04:51,326 --> 00:04:53,805
Praise be, my boys! Come on!

28
00:04:59,646 --> 00:05:03,285
A conquest cannot be performed
only with swords, sisters.

29
00:05:03,766 --> 00:05:07,925
It's performed with bread, meals and prayers.

30
00:05:08,406 --> 00:05:11,263
Every ember in the fire
and every bread in the table...

31
00:05:11,275 --> 00:05:14,205
...should have the
smell of conquest on them.

32
00:05:14,486 --> 00:05:15,605
Right?

33
00:05:16,646 --> 00:05:17,485
Come on.

34
00:05:19,806 --> 00:05:21,485
Come on, my dear.

35
00:05:22,366 --> 00:05:24,125
Are you helping too?

36
00:05:25,966 --> 00:05:28,485
A bride is always like her
mother-in-law, they say.

37
00:05:29,126 --> 00:05:30,525
It seems they are right.

38
00:05:30,886 --> 00:05:32,405
Praise be.

39
00:05:38,126 --> 00:05:39,405
Who are you?

40
00:05:41,126 --> 00:05:42,165
Are you..

41
00:05:43,446 --> 00:05:44,765
A nomad?

42
00:05:46,166 --> 00:05:46,845
Yes.

43
00:05:47,606 --> 00:05:49,365
I'm here to get to know Osman Bey.

44
00:05:49,526 --> 00:05:50,965
Osman Bey isn't here.

45
00:05:51,326 --> 00:05:53,045
He's gone to meet the emperor.

46
00:05:55,566 --> 00:05:59,085
Osman Bey is powerful enough
to meet the emperor, huh?

47
00:06:00,726 --> 00:06:02,885
You don't know Osman Bey, obviously.

48
00:06:03,446 --> 00:06:05,525
He's the best in the frontiers.

49
00:06:07,726 --> 00:06:11,525
Do you use an axe?

50
00:06:15,566 --> 00:06:17,365
Can you teach me how to use it?

51
00:06:17,686 --> 00:06:19,525
Tell me, double-sworded boy.

52
00:06:20,006 --> 00:06:21,325
What is your name?

53
00:06:23,486 --> 00:06:24,845
Ghazi Alp.

54
00:06:26,286 --> 00:06:30,515
Alright. Okay.
I'll teach you, but...

55
00:06:31,366 --> 00:06:34,445
...you need to tell me about
the news in the frontiers.

56
00:06:35,206 --> 00:06:36,485
I will.

57
00:06:53,366 --> 00:06:56,685
The fate of the frontiers
will be redetermined in Iznik.

58
00:06:56,766 --> 00:07:02,925
Let's see whether this talk
will bring benefits or troubles.

59
00:07:05,126 --> 00:07:06,365
My Bey.

60
00:07:07,006 --> 00:07:09,805
Why do you think the emperor invited us here?

61
00:07:10,246 --> 00:07:12,045
Games never end in these lands.

62
00:07:12,326 --> 00:07:14,245
A new order will be provided.

63
00:07:14,686 --> 00:07:17,845
Let's see which side we will take.

64
00:07:18,126 --> 00:07:19,845
Allah is with us, my Bey.

65
00:07:20,446 --> 00:07:22,245
The rest doesn't matter.

66
00:07:44,606 --> 00:07:48,245
The precious and great city of the Roman Empire.

67
00:07:48,406 --> 00:07:52,125
The ancient town of Christians
that has never been conquered.

68
00:07:52,126 --> 00:07:54,045
Welcome to Nikea, Osman Bey.

69
00:07:54,636 --> 00:07:57,237
Thanks for welcoming us
in the city that our ancestor

70
00:07:57,249 --> 00:08:00,515
Suleyman Shah, son of
Kutalmis Bey, once conquered,

71
00:08:00,515 --> 00:08:01,635
..commander.

72
00:08:05,566 --> 00:08:09,085
Our mighty emperor Andronikos
is expecting you, Osman Bey.

73
00:08:29,646 --> 00:08:31,125
Let's go.

74
00:08:42,846 --> 00:08:44,685
Praise be, alps!

75
00:08:44,806 --> 00:08:46,925
Come on, warriors! Cling your swords!

76
00:08:53,366 --> 00:08:54,885
Faster.

77
00:08:58,126 --> 00:09:00,325
Watch me, man.

78
00:09:07,526 --> 00:09:09,485
I use double swords very well.

79
00:09:09,806 --> 00:09:11,565
But I can't use an axe.

80
00:09:11,686 --> 00:09:13,525
I trained a lot.

81
00:09:17,486 --> 00:09:19,165
But I keep dropping it.

82
00:09:19,726 --> 00:09:21,885
Tell me what my mistake is.

83
00:09:26,406 --> 00:09:28,645
You hold the axe too tightly.

84
00:09:28,886 --> 00:09:33,045
You shouldn't hold it
tightly but in a balanced way.

85
00:09:35,006 --> 00:09:36,805
Watch me.

86
00:09:58,766 --> 00:10:00,325
Praise be.

87
00:10:00,326 --> 00:10:04,045
Brothers, who is that stranger swinging the axe?

88
00:10:04,286 --> 00:10:07,885
I haven't seen him before
but he's good at using an axe.

89
00:10:10,966 --> 00:10:13,005
Tell me, Aykurt Cavus.

90
00:10:13,486 --> 00:10:15,765
Can you beat that man?

91
00:10:15,926 --> 00:10:17,485
Let's see.

92
00:10:18,846 --> 00:10:22,085
Uncle, what have you done?

93
00:10:26,126 --> 00:10:30,205
The axe isn't only your weapon
but also your arms and wings.

94
00:10:30,606 --> 00:10:34,765
If you think that way, you will never drop it.

95
00:10:34,966 --> 00:10:36,485
I got it, uncle.

96
00:10:36,846 --> 00:10:39,965
You are a great fighter.

97
00:10:40,406 --> 00:10:41,845
Praise be.

98
00:10:43,766 --> 00:10:46,045
Peace be upon you.

99
00:10:49,286 --> 00:10:51,405
Peace be upon you too.

100
00:10:51,406 --> 00:10:55,405
So you swing your axe well, old man.

101
00:10:55,406 --> 00:10:57,885
Praising myself would be childish.

102
00:10:58,366 --> 00:11:04,285
But for sure, no man
has defeated me until today.

103
00:11:10,886 --> 00:11:16,165
Then come and show your bravery.

104
00:11:17,326 --> 00:11:20,845
We never stayed back from practicing.

105
00:11:20,926 --> 00:11:23,605
Come on, show your skills.

106
00:11:23,606 --> 00:11:29,045
Come on then. In the name of Allah, 
the merciful, the compassionate.

107
00:11:33,046 --> 00:11:34,845
Come on brother.

108
00:12:02,446 --> 00:12:03,885
Brother!

109
00:12:32,086 --> 00:12:35,085
Good, good.

110
00:12:39,366 --> 00:12:41,365
Hay Praise be.

111
00:12:42,766 --> 00:12:45,605
Praise be.

112
00:12:45,606 --> 00:12:47,565
Hay Praise be.

113
00:12:47,566 --> 00:12:52,565
They called you old, but you defeated two Alps.

114
00:12:52,566 --> 00:12:54,165
Thanks.

115
00:12:54,366 --> 00:12:58,485
Your hearts are very strong,
valiants. You fight well.

116
00:12:59,206 --> 00:13:01,365
Thank you, thank you.

117
00:13:01,366 --> 00:13:03,725
Tell... tell me.

118
00:13:03,726 --> 00:13:11,445
What is the name of the valiant who
defeated me and dropped my mace?

119
00:13:12,526 --> 00:13:16,405
An Alp who fights in the way of
glorification of the word of Allah.

120
00:13:16,566 --> 00:13:18,085
That's all.

121
00:13:18,086 --> 00:13:19,685
Hay Praise be.

122
00:13:19,686 --> 00:13:23,045
Praise be.

123
00:13:23,046 --> 00:13:24,605
Alright.

124
00:13:24,966 --> 00:13:30,885
I wanted to see Osman Bey, but I
heard he went to meet the emperor.

125
00:13:30,886 --> 00:13:33,365
Does anyone know why he went?

126
00:13:37,006 --> 00:13:41,725
We don't know why he went.
We are also waiting for our Bey.

127
00:13:41,726 --> 00:13:46,165
We will know our target when Osman Bey returns.

128
00:14:06,606 --> 00:14:08,325
Osman Bey.

129
00:14:10,966 --> 00:14:15,245
Seeing you coming here with peace...

130
00:14:18,686 --> 00:14:22,325
I am very happy you accepted my invitation.

131
00:14:22,486 --> 00:14:28,085
Coming to the West is our never ending rule.

132
00:14:28,206 --> 00:14:30,805
Emperor Andronikos.

133
00:14:32,726 --> 00:14:36,565
This table is prepared for you. Please, come.

134
00:15:01,606 --> 00:15:05,965
Your strength is still with you like your rule.

135
00:15:06,046 --> 00:15:10,525
Time treated you well. You haven't aged a bit.

136
00:15:11,126 --> 00:15:16,565
Wars or the tricks of Byzantium don't tire us.

137
00:15:16,646 --> 00:15:20,925
Despite the failure of
your tricks and attempts...

138
00:15:21,086 --> 00:15:27,765
...even though you gave Bursa to
the Mongols with Claudius' rebellion...

139
00:15:30,286 --> 00:15:32,445
...I see you are still very happy.

140
00:15:33,406 --> 00:15:38,125
You are talking about the
thousands-year-old Roman Empire, Osman Bey.

141
00:15:41,446 --> 00:15:48,525
Even though we made plans and sometimes
fell into traps, we always stood strong.

142
00:15:49,686 --> 00:15:52,325
Because our foundations are solid.

143
00:15:55,006 --> 00:15:57,725
I own half the world.

144
00:15:58,246 --> 00:16:00,605
With the roads we built..

145
00:16:00,606 --> 00:16:07,245
...and unique buildings like Hagia Sophia,
we brought civilization to the world.

146
00:16:08,446 --> 00:16:15,285
And also, Byzantium is not
the only state that lost things.

147
00:16:16,206 --> 00:16:17,645
I heard it.

148
00:16:18,126 --> 00:16:22,725
The Ilkhanid Mongols took your tribe.

149
00:16:31,926 --> 00:16:33,805
Even if the Turk loses...

150
00:16:37,726 --> 00:16:41,165
...he never stops until he
takes back what he lost.

151
00:16:43,166 --> 00:16:44,925
So, Andronikos.

152
00:16:46,206 --> 00:16:49,605
My ancestors who once
spread fear in your empire...

153
00:16:49,926 --> 00:16:54,445
...Cagri and Tugrul Bey, you know them well.

154
00:16:54,886 --> 00:16:57,245
They lost their tribes.

155
00:16:57,646 --> 00:16:59,965
The Ghaznavids and the Karakhanids...

156
00:17:01,486 --> 00:17:03,685
You underestimated them.

157
00:17:03,926 --> 00:17:09,405
But my ancestors' dreams were so strong that..

158
00:17:11,286 --> 00:17:15,885
...you learned this in the
hardest way at Manzikert.

159
00:17:19,445 --> 00:17:25,805
Since that time, the Turk's goal
and dream have never changed.

160
00:17:25,925 --> 00:17:28,965
Even if we lose our tribes...

161
00:17:31,086 --> 00:17:33,085
In the hardest times...

162
00:17:33,806 --> 00:17:35,725
We know how to rise again.

163
00:17:38,326 --> 00:17:39,205
And..

164
00:17:40,966 --> 00:17:45,565
We always know how to establish a state.

165
00:17:47,246 --> 00:17:53,125
Now it's not about personal
resurrection or salvation, Osman Bey.

166
00:17:53,486 --> 00:17:58,765
The situation requires an alliance
for the future of the frontiers...

167
00:17:58,766 --> 00:18:02,685
Byzantium and the Kayi tribe.

168
00:18:06,126 --> 00:18:07,845
Emperor..

169
00:18:08,406 --> 00:18:13,525
...when I saved your life, you offered me peace.

170
00:18:15,486 --> 00:18:17,325
But that peace...

171
00:18:19,486 --> 00:18:22,285
...only brought us betrayal.

172
00:18:30,566 --> 00:18:33,525
While the Mongols are
bringing their army here...

173
00:18:33,526 --> 00:18:37,565
...betrayal of the alliance would
bring disaster to the frontiers.

174
00:18:38,286 --> 00:18:39,885
On the contrary...

175
00:18:40,286 --> 00:18:48,245
...my wish is for this alliance, which
started for defense, to grow through trade.

176
00:18:49,446 --> 00:18:51,605
We can establish a common marketplace.

177
00:18:51,846 --> 00:18:54,845
We can trade without paying taxes.

178
00:18:55,966 --> 00:18:57,805
Did I understand correctly?

179
00:18:57,806 --> 00:19:00,485
In this region, in these frontiers..

180
00:19:01,486 --> 00:19:05,645
...Kayi's growth and its development...

181
00:19:07,846 --> 00:19:09,965
do not scare you?

182
00:19:09,966 --> 00:19:12,965
Rome is not scared of anyone, Osman Bey.

183
00:19:16,166 --> 00:19:21,285
As long as you stay loyal to the alliance
and do not wage war against the West.

184
00:19:22,046 --> 00:19:25,845
If Kayi becomes strong within its own borders...

185
00:19:25,846 --> 00:19:30,085
...it will also protect our eastern borders.

186
00:19:31,006 --> 00:19:36,525
That Mongol, who caused us to lose Bursa
and who is served by that dog Claudius...

187
00:19:36,846 --> 00:19:39,645
If you defeat Kucar, Osman Bey...

188
00:19:39,806 --> 00:19:45,445
...then we will no longer be
enemies, we will be friends forever.

189
00:19:45,446 --> 00:19:47,925
So, Emperor...

190
00:19:49,166 --> 00:19:51,645
..you say you fear no one.

191
00:19:53,446 --> 00:19:57,725
But your rebellious commander Claudius...

192
00:19:58,806 --> 00:20:00,445
...you fear him.

193
00:20:00,446 --> 00:20:02,445
He is a traitor.

194
00:20:02,806 --> 00:20:08,525
It's not about fear, the real issue
is the wound he gave to Byzantium.

195
00:20:08,526 --> 00:20:11,725
Let's say I prefer an enemy
who looks me in the eye...

196
00:20:11,726 --> 00:20:16,405
...over a traitor who stabs me in the back.

197
00:20:33,646 --> 00:20:39,405
You're a weak Byzantine
soldier, but not too bad.

198
00:20:48,566 --> 00:20:51,285
You... You..

199
00:20:51,606 --> 00:20:57,325
You are too weak to even hurt my fingernail.

200
00:21:25,926 --> 00:21:29,685
Kucar, I am not your enemy.

201
00:21:29,926 --> 00:21:32,325
Go and take your anger out on Osman.

202
00:21:37,886 --> 00:21:44,805
Not just Osman, none of
the Muslims on this land...

203
00:21:45,046 --> 00:21:49,525
...will be able to escape my wrath.

204
00:21:54,726 --> 00:22:01,245
When my army arrives, no
heads will remain on shoulders!

205
00:22:28,286 --> 00:22:29,765
So..

206
00:22:31,566 --> 00:22:34,805
...you want me to defeat our
common enemy, the Mongols.

207
00:22:35,806 --> 00:22:39,605
You say that in this way our
friendship will last forever?

208
00:22:44,446 --> 00:22:47,845
In return for our friendship,
I want an army from you.

209
00:22:50,246 --> 00:22:53,645
If I weren't fighting with the
Kipchaks in the Balkans...

210
00:22:53,766 --> 00:22:56,805
...I would place my army on the frontiers.

211
00:22:57,526 --> 00:23:01,845
But in this alliance, my duty
is to open my treasury to you...

212
00:23:02,246 --> 00:23:04,645
...so you can strengthen your army.

213
00:23:04,646 --> 00:23:07,125
You can't win this war with gold.

214
00:23:07,806 --> 00:23:09,885
If you won't give an army...

215
00:23:10,606 --> 00:23:15,525
...then you will give more than gold.

216
00:23:16,366 --> 00:23:18,445
Tell me, Osman Bey.

217
00:23:18,966 --> 00:23:24,005
What do you want from me
as the price of this alliance?

218
00:23:24,926 --> 00:23:27,525
Along with gold...

219
00:23:27,526 --> 00:23:32,565
...I want to rule the Karacabes
Castle and all the lands around it.

220
00:23:32,726 --> 00:23:38,125
Karacabes Castle is one
of the lifelines of my empire.

221
00:23:38,126 --> 00:23:42,845
Will you take a piece of my flesh
by using our alliance, Osman Bey?

222
00:23:42,846 --> 00:23:47,925
You already lost your lifeline Bursa,
to your rebellious commander Claudius.

223
00:23:49,566 --> 00:23:53,245
Now this precious city, Iznik, and the others...

224
00:23:54,006 --> 00:23:56,725
Do you want to give them to the Mongols?

225
00:23:57,766 --> 00:23:59,805
If not..

226
00:24:01,086 --> 00:24:03,765
...then you will give me what I want.

227
00:24:05,726 --> 00:24:08,165
And I will stand against the Mongols.

228
00:24:08,846 --> 00:24:13,125
I will send Kucar away from these lands.

229
00:24:14,206 --> 00:24:17,805
With my life and my army,
I will stand against them all.

230
00:24:26,086 --> 00:24:28,365
Your rebellious commander Claudius..

231
00:24:29,366 --> 00:24:33,805
When he becomes weak, you will destroy him too.

232
00:24:35,566 --> 00:24:37,605
Agreed, Osman Bey.

233
00:24:38,446 --> 00:24:42,245
The gold and the Karacabes Castle are yours.

234
00:24:42,646 --> 00:24:47,325
You handle Kucar, and I will handle Claudius.

235
00:24:47,326 --> 00:24:54,605
And I hope both our trade and
our friendship will last forever.

236
00:24:54,606 --> 00:24:56,285
God willing.

237
00:24:58,006 --> 00:25:00,085
God willing Emperor.

238
00:25:10,966 --> 00:25:17,405
My soldiers are coming
from the borders of Enguru.

239
00:25:17,526 --> 00:25:24,005
They travel quietly day and night.

240
00:25:25,806 --> 00:25:27,325
Kucar..

241
00:25:27,406 --> 00:25:34,005
...with your army and my
soldiers, we will rule all the frontiers.

242
00:25:34,846 --> 00:25:39,845
Then we will ride our horses
to west and rule all the lands.

243
00:25:44,566 --> 00:25:46,605
Exciting.

244
00:25:48,286 --> 00:25:50,245
Then what?

245
00:25:51,206 --> 00:25:52,645
Then..

246
00:25:53,526 --> 00:26:00,765
I will dethrone that old
Emperor and sit on the throne.

247
00:26:01,926 --> 00:26:04,125
I will rule Rome.

248
00:26:09,246 --> 00:26:11,085
You

249
00:26:16,726 --> 00:26:21,365
You will be nothing...

250
00:26:22,126 --> 00:26:28,245
...more than a commander sleeping
on a throne under my shadow and...

251
00:26:28,246 --> 00:26:34,365
...under the protection of the Khan
of Khans Olcaytu Khan, Claudius.

252
00:27:17,926 --> 00:27:20,365
Everything is done, right? I want no mistakes.

253
00:27:20,366 --> 00:27:22,485
Everything should be ready for our army.

254
00:27:22,606 --> 00:27:25,005
It's as you ordered, mother. Done.

255
00:27:25,766 --> 00:27:29,285
Mother, these carts are going with the others.

256
00:27:32,526 --> 00:27:33,645
Bring it.

257
00:27:40,006 --> 00:27:42,045
Good. Cover it.

258
00:27:43,686 --> 00:27:45,565
Let me see those.

259
00:27:52,286 --> 00:27:52,845
Good.

260
00:27:53,006 --> 00:27:55,485
They're all going to the army camp in Karaorman.

261
00:27:55,566 --> 00:27:57,845
Place the materials in the most shadowed spot.

262
00:27:57,886 --> 00:27:59,965
-As you order, Bala Hatun.
-Come on.

263
00:28:03,806 --> 00:28:05,365
May your work be easy, hatuns!

264
00:28:05,486 --> 00:28:07,485
-Welcome, Bala Hatun.
-Thank you.

265
00:28:07,606 --> 00:28:08,845
Welcome.

266
00:28:09,006 --> 00:28:10,365
-Welcome.
-Are you well?

267
00:28:10,406 --> 00:28:11,885
Thanks to Allah, I am.

268
00:28:11,926 --> 00:28:13,405
-May your work be easy.
-We're all working.

269
00:28:13,526 --> 00:28:15,565
Praise be, Praise be. May your work be easy.

270
00:28:39,686 --> 00:28:41,645
The same man, mother.

271
00:28:43,126 --> 00:28:46,045
He was watching us while
we were going into the woods.

272
00:28:46,166 --> 00:28:47,925
But we didn't care.

273
00:28:55,006 --> 00:28:57,605
He's been watching us
since we came to the tribe.

274
00:28:58,326 --> 00:29:01,445
He was walking around the carts yesterday.

275
00:29:05,406 --> 00:29:08,125
He may be the spy who informs Begum.

276
00:29:08,726 --> 00:29:11,045
I'm sure. That's him.

277
00:29:15,646 --> 00:29:17,485
First, we will follow

278
00:29:17,966 --> 00:29:21,325
Let's see if he meets Begum.

279
00:29:25,166 --> 00:29:26,805
I'll manage the preparations.

280
00:29:26,806 --> 00:29:30,445
Girls, you follow him with the alps.

281
00:29:30,566 --> 00:29:32,365
Be cautious, though.

282
00:29:32,606 --> 00:29:36,125
Don't let him realize you're following.

283
00:29:37,566 --> 00:29:39,285
What if he meets Begum?

284
00:29:39,806 --> 00:29:43,005
You'll take that snake
and bring her to our tribe.

285
00:29:44,086 --> 00:29:46,325
-As you order, mother.
-As you order, mother.

286
00:29:46,326 --> 00:29:47,565
Come on, girls.

287
00:29:52,126 --> 00:29:54,045
Let's see where he goes.

288
00:30:11,686 --> 00:30:16,565
Here is the gold that our mighty emperor
Andronikos promised you, Osman Bey.

289
00:30:19,806 --> 00:30:21,845
Alps, take it.

290
00:30:24,406 --> 00:30:25,845
Excuse me.

291
00:30:32,486 --> 00:30:33,405
My Bey.

292
00:30:34,686 --> 00:30:36,285
Forgive me.

293
00:30:37,846 --> 00:30:39,845
Demanding a castle is one thing.

294
00:30:40,086 --> 00:30:45,845
But going to a war with that
heathen's gold... I don't know, my Bey.

295
00:30:46,726 --> 00:30:49,405
I don't feel comfortable either, my Bey.

296
00:30:49,526 --> 00:30:51,125
Don't worry.

297
00:30:51,566 --> 00:30:55,525
The gold is for Kucar's head.

298
00:30:56,366 --> 00:30:58,805
Well... We divided Byzantine.

299
00:30:59,366 --> 00:31:03,165
Kucar and Gladius will be next.

300
00:31:03,686 --> 00:31:05,365
You meet Gladius.

301
00:31:05,926 --> 00:31:07,925
Tell him we want to have a deal.

302
00:31:08,046 --> 00:31:11,365
He should come to Akcapinar tomorrow.

303
00:31:11,566 --> 00:31:12,845
Okay, my Bey.

304
00:31:13,046 --> 00:31:14,645
Tell Cerkutay.

305
00:31:14,926 --> 00:31:18,765
The castle of Karacabes will belong to Turks.

306
00:31:18,846 --> 00:31:21,285
He should capture and then reinforce it.

307
00:31:21,326 --> 00:31:22,885
As you order, my Bey

308
00:32:10,606 --> 00:32:12,165
He's waiting for someone.

309
00:32:12,886 --> 00:32:14,405
Shall we make him speak?

310
00:32:15,006 --> 00:32:17,805
If he is Begum's spy, he must know where she is.

311
00:32:19,046 --> 00:32:20,245
I don't think so.

312
00:32:21,326 --> 00:32:25,165
Begum must have taken measures
in case her spy gets caught.

313
00:32:28,926 --> 00:32:30,285
No doubt.

314
00:32:30,886 --> 00:32:32,365
That's her spy.

315
00:32:33,246 --> 00:32:36,325
She has to pay for the
things that she made us suffer.

316
00:32:36,486 --> 00:32:37,805
We'll wait and see.

317
00:32:38,966 --> 00:32:40,965
If it is Begum who he is waiting for,

318
00:32:41,566 --> 00:32:44,445
...she won't be able to run off this time.

319
00:32:52,166 --> 00:32:55,765
Many khans, many rulers...

320
00:32:57,406 --> 00:33:01,285
...many commanders and soldiers, Turks have had.

321
00:33:03,606 --> 00:33:10,005
Some struggled behind Tengri Mountains in Hotan.

322
00:33:10,286 --> 00:33:17,245
Some, in the west, made the
enemy think he was the scourge.

323
00:33:18,486 --> 00:33:21,605
Osman Bey is one of those great rulers, man.

324
00:33:22,286 --> 00:33:28,405
He is a brave man who hits the cruel and all
the heathens like a scourge in the frontiers.

325
00:33:31,006 --> 00:33:36,285
You must be happy that you live
under the wings of such a brave Bey.

326
00:33:37,006 --> 00:33:38,685
Thank Allah.

327
00:33:41,486 --> 00:33:45,645
With the guidance of Osman
Bey, the ruler in the frontiers,

328
00:33:45,766 --> 00:33:52,485
...those will protect all the orphans
and the ones in need, God willing.

329
00:33:52,566 --> 00:33:54,485
God willing.
God willing.

330
00:33:55,126 --> 00:34:01,405
Once upon a time, I was the
fellow of a courageous Bey.

331
00:34:03,806 --> 00:34:10,085
The sword he lifted towards the sky
became a sun raining fire on the cruel...

332
00:34:11,045 --> 00:34:14,804
...and cooled the innocent with its shadow.

333
00:34:17,326 --> 00:34:21,685
He was a Bey who brought
order and justice wherever he went.

334
00:34:22,565 --> 00:34:24,245
Which Bey is that?

335
00:34:25,326 --> 00:34:26,965
Tell me, man.

336
00:34:27,406 --> 00:34:30,565
The one who settled in
these lands with his tribe

337
00:34:30,726 --> 00:34:36,804
...avoided nothing at all to make
this land a homeland for Turks,

338
00:34:37,326 --> 00:34:42,965
...proved that Turks would prevail
forever against the whole world...

339
00:34:43,806 --> 00:34:47,125
...and became a soldier for the Islam world.

340
00:34:49,525 --> 00:34:51,565
He was Ertugrul Ghazi.

341
00:34:52,606 --> 00:34:54,284
Ertugrul Ghazi.

342
00:34:54,926 --> 00:34:57,805
-He said Ertugrul Ghazi.
-Ertugrul Ghazi.

343
00:35:00,006 --> 00:35:02,245
What does this old man say, brothers?

344
00:35:04,086 --> 00:35:11,085
Were you one of the soldiers of
Ertugrul Ghazi, Osman Bey's father?

345
00:35:11,606 --> 00:35:13,405
Osman Bey.

346
00:35:26,006 --> 00:35:27,925
What's going on here?

347
00:35:29,566 --> 00:35:31,525
Who are you? Show me your face.

348
00:35:52,286 --> 00:35:53,765
How?

349
00:36:10,846 --> 00:36:12,645
How is that possible?

350
00:36:16,486 --> 00:36:18,125
Turgut Ghazi.

351
00:36:18,166 --> 00:36:20,085
Yes.

352
00:36:35,326 --> 00:36:37,245
Tell me, Osman Bey.

353
00:36:37,566 --> 00:36:40,605
Do you have a place in your tribe...

354
00:36:42,646 --> 00:36:44,445
...and in your army for this alp?

355
00:36:44,886 --> 00:36:46,565
What are you even saying?

356
00:36:47,086 --> 00:36:51,285
This tribe, tent and army is already yours.

357
00:36:51,526 --> 00:36:53,245
Welcome, Turgut Ghazi.

358
00:36:53,366 --> 00:36:55,525
Thank you, good to see you.

359
00:36:55,766 --> 00:36:59,125
Praise be.

360
00:36:59,526 --> 00:37:01,285
Praise be.

361
00:37:01,726 --> 00:37:05,485
Praise be...
My father's fellow.

362
00:37:05,846 --> 00:37:10,005
-Turgut Ghazi, the bravest of the brave!
-Thank you, Osman Bey. Thank you.

363
00:37:11,006 --> 00:37:12,445
Come with me.

364
00:37:13,126 --> 00:37:16,045
The person you see, my children.

365
00:37:16,286 --> 00:37:20,605
...is Turgut Ghazi who suffered a lot for Kayi.

366
00:37:25,006 --> 00:37:28,805
Sisters, prepare a tent for
him and show great respect.

367
00:37:30,406 --> 00:37:35,765
You are the man with whose
brave stories we grew up, huh?

368
00:37:37,286 --> 00:37:42,565
Turgut Ghazi, whose axe fought together
with Bamsi Bey's double swords, huh?

369
00:37:43,875 --> 00:37:44,875
Right.

370
00:37:45,806 --> 00:37:49,765
Well... My son Orhan. My son Alaaddin.

371
00:37:50,406 --> 00:37:52,165
Praise be.

372
00:37:52,886 --> 00:37:54,605
Praise be.

373
00:37:58,766 --> 00:38:02,645
Ertugrul Bey's family have grown bigger.

374
00:38:03,366 --> 00:38:05,605
Praise be, boys.

375
00:38:16,406 --> 00:38:19,005
The preparation made for the army has set out.

376
00:38:19,046 --> 00:38:22,045
They're going to keep it in a
hidden camp in Karaorman.

377
00:38:22,046 --> 00:38:23,685
Karaorman, huh?

378
00:38:24,846 --> 00:38:27,365
All their preparation will go for nothing.

379
00:38:27,526 --> 00:38:30,445
Their army won't be able
to have anything to eat.

380
00:38:31,046 --> 00:38:34,965
Alps, get ready. We're going to Karaorman.

381
00:38:36,446 --> 00:38:41,605
Vural, go back to their tribe
and let me know their every step.

382
00:38:47,846 --> 00:38:49,965
Alps, watch out.

383
00:39:05,486 --> 00:39:08,965
It's time to pay for what you did, Begum.

384
00:39:13,206 --> 00:39:18,045
You all have come to me to pass away, huh?

385
00:39:21,846 --> 00:39:24,525
Alps, attack!

386
00:39:42,206 --> 00:39:43,965
Halime, protect yourself.

387
00:40:26,246 --> 00:40:27,605
Begum

388
00:40:34,766 --> 00:40:36,485
You will pay, Begum.

389
00:40:36,766 --> 00:40:38,725
You will pay for everything.

390
00:40:39,166 --> 00:40:42,805
I did everything because
of the injustice I suffered.

391
00:40:45,126 --> 00:40:48,925
You thought you could run off?

392
00:40:49,846 --> 00:40:51,805
You attempted to...

393
00:40:52,166 --> 00:40:54,805
You attempted to burn my mother alive.

394
00:40:55,766 --> 00:40:58,885
You attempted to burn my mother alive, huh?

395
00:40:59,086 --> 00:41:02,005
I will kill you. I'll kill you.

396
00:41:03,486 --> 00:41:05,525
-I will kill you.
-Fatma. Fatma!

397
00:41:05,806 --> 00:41:08,245
-I'll kill you!
-Fatma, stop that!

398
00:41:08,446 --> 00:41:10,125
-Let me kill her.
-Fatma, stop!

399
00:41:10,286 --> 00:41:12,685
Let her kill. She deserves to die.

400
00:41:13,166 --> 00:41:15,685
-I will kill her.
-Fatma!

401
00:41:16,966 --> 00:41:19,565
It's mother and father who deserve to kill her.

402
00:41:19,606 --> 00:41:21,605
Will you really take it from them?

403
00:41:24,766 --> 00:41:27,605
Sisters, tie her up!

404
00:41:28,126 --> 00:41:29,725
We're taking her to our tribe.

405
00:41:37,526 --> 00:41:40,205
Come on. Let's go.

406
00:41:59,646 --> 00:42:01,765
This sword...

407
00:42:16,006 --> 00:42:20,565
With my brothers Bamsi and Dogan...

408
00:42:20,966 --> 00:42:23,045
...we always...

409
00:42:24,806 --> 00:42:29,645
...rode to the blessed
destinations this sword showed.

410
00:42:35,006 --> 00:42:39,325
The owner of this sword
taught us the faith, my Osman.

411
00:42:45,566 --> 00:42:48,205
May my Ertugrul Bey rest in heaven...

412
00:43:00,006 --> 00:43:04,845
This generation owes you so much.

413
00:43:14,406 --> 00:43:21,005
Our generation owes you and
the many valiants you mentioned.

414
00:43:21,166 --> 00:43:22,925
Ha, Turgut Ghazi?

415
00:43:22,926 --> 00:43:24,485
Thank you.

416
00:43:24,766 --> 00:43:26,485
Tell me.

417
00:43:26,566 --> 00:43:29,005
Where have you been all this time?

418
00:43:29,006 --> 00:43:30,765
What did you do?

419
00:43:30,766 --> 00:43:33,805
We thought you passed
away from this mortal world.

420
00:43:33,806 --> 00:43:35,245
Tell me.

421
00:43:35,606 --> 00:43:37,605
I was in the Balkans.

422
00:43:38,886 --> 00:43:45,645
I brought you the respect and
greetings of many Turks who settled there.

423
00:43:46,606 --> 00:43:49,605
They are waiting to hear your horse's footsteps.

424
00:43:50,086 --> 00:43:53,325
They are all waiting for you.

425
00:44:00,486 --> 00:44:04,125
Tell me. What did you do in those lands?

426
00:44:06,126 --> 00:44:10,845
My Ertugrul Bey gave me a secret
duty, that's why I had to disappear.

427
00:44:11,046 --> 00:44:13,405
I was there for that duty.

428
00:44:13,406 --> 00:44:16,725
I was a companion to Saru Saltuk for years.

429
00:44:17,406 --> 00:44:21,485
We kept struggling and
working for the cause of Islam.

430
00:44:23,566 --> 00:44:26,445
My wise father.

431
00:44:26,686 --> 00:44:32,165
Even while fighting in the fire
circle, he did not forget the Balkans.

432
00:44:33,846 --> 00:44:37,805
Now my last wish is to...

433
00:44:38,366 --> 00:44:42,656
...dedicate the rest
of my life to the path of

434
00:44:42,668 --> 00:44:47,245
Osman Bey, who fights
in the fire like his father.

435
00:44:52,366 --> 00:44:56,645
You will be a mountain behind
me like you were for my father, huh?

436
00:44:56,646 --> 00:44:58,965
For sure.

437
00:45:02,806 --> 00:45:04,285
Hay Praise be.

438
00:45:08,566 --> 00:45:11,245
My uncle, the legacy of my father.

439
00:45:12,526 --> 00:45:15,645
Thank you my Osman. Thank you.

440
00:45:23,886 --> 00:45:26,965
You will be nothing...

441
00:45:26,966 --> 00:45:33,565
...more than a commander sleeping
on a throne under my shadow and...

442
00:45:33,766 --> 00:45:39,685
...under the protection of the Khan
of Khans Olcaytu Khan, Claudius.

443
00:45:46,486 --> 00:45:49,165
So I am under your shadow, Kucar?

444
00:45:52,966 --> 00:45:56,725
You dirty pedicular pig of the steppe.

445
00:45:59,846 --> 00:46:05,165
I will use everyone and
everything until I don't need them.

446
00:47:02,086 --> 00:47:04,925
You will pay for this, Kucar.

447
00:47:06,246 --> 00:47:10,525
My rule you thought was under
your shadow will be your end.

448
00:47:19,286 --> 00:47:20,925
Walk!

449
00:47:21,046 --> 00:47:23,165
Walk Begum!

450
00:47:25,566 --> 00:47:26,885
Traitor!

451
00:47:27,486 --> 00:47:29,365
Walk!

452
00:47:38,726 --> 00:47:40,405
Begum...

453
00:47:42,126 --> 00:47:45,285
You snake... So it was you, huh?

454
00:47:46,286 --> 00:47:48,125
Come here!

455
00:47:52,126 --> 00:47:53,685
Do you remember?

456
00:47:53,686 --> 00:47:56,405
You tried to imprison me in my own tribe.

457
00:47:56,406 --> 00:47:59,765
I told you that day you
would go where you deserved!

458
00:47:59,766 --> 00:48:04,885
Now that day has come, Begum! Get up!

459
00:48:05,246 --> 00:48:08,045
I told you, you can not take anything from me.

460
00:48:08,046 --> 00:48:12,725
You tried to kill me and
made my children suffer.

461
00:48:12,966 --> 00:48:14,125
Get up

462
00:48:14,126 --> 00:48:15,325
Stop it!

463
00:48:15,326 --> 00:48:18,365
Get up Begum, get up!

464
00:48:18,606 --> 00:48:22,405
This is for the cruelty you did to my people!

465
00:48:22,966 --> 00:48:25,765
Get up Begum, get up!

466
00:48:26,206 --> 00:48:30,645
This is for attempting to hurt my children!

467
00:48:42,086 --> 00:48:43,285
Get up!

468
00:48:43,286 --> 00:48:44,765
Stop it!

469
00:48:48,166 --> 00:48:52,685
And this is because you
set your eyes on my family!

470
00:48:53,726 --> 00:48:55,165
Get up! Get up Begum!

471
00:48:55,166 --> 00:48:56,765
Do not disgrace me here Bala!

472
00:48:56,766 --> 00:48:59,405
You are already a disgrace!

473
00:48:59,406 --> 00:49:01,525
Kill me! Kill me already!

474
00:49:01,526 --> 00:49:04,325
Don't worry, the end you deserve will come.

475
00:49:10,126 --> 00:49:13,885
Kill me! Kill me already!

476
00:49:13,886 --> 00:49:15,605
Attention

477
00:49:18,846 --> 00:49:20,605
Osman Bey!

478
00:49:28,206 --> 00:49:29,685
My Bey

479
00:49:33,766 --> 00:49:35,685
My Bey, forgive me!

480
00:49:35,686 --> 00:49:37,685
Forgive me, my Bey!

481
00:49:38,246 --> 00:49:40,325
I regret it, my Bey!

482
00:49:40,446 --> 00:49:42,685
Please, forgive me!

483
00:49:43,646 --> 00:49:45,845
You liar...

484
00:49:55,566 --> 00:49:57,245
Bring her into the tent.

485
00:50:12,286 --> 00:50:14,005
Commander Claudius...

486
00:50:27,366 --> 00:50:29,685
Master Claudius is listening to you.

487
00:50:33,926 --> 00:50:41,445
The ruler of Yenisehir, Sogut,
Karacahisar, Atranos, Lefke,

488
00:50:41,446 --> 00:50:48,005
Karadin and Akhisar, the sun
of the frontiers and of all Turks...

489
00:50:52,966 --> 00:50:54,645
I heard enough.

490
00:51:30,206 --> 00:51:34,925
Doesn't it scare you that I can kill you?

491
00:51:35,846 --> 00:51:42,285
I am here by the order of the ruler
Osman Bey, protector of all Turkmens.

492
00:51:46,046 --> 00:51:48,925
And the answer of your question, Commander.

493
00:51:54,006 --> 00:51:57,245
Since I am wearing my
faith in Allah like armor...

494
00:51:59,406 --> 00:52:02,205
I am never afraid of death.

495
00:52:04,566 --> 00:52:07,645
That happens to faithless people like you.

496
00:52:12,966 --> 00:52:19,285
You Turks mistake ignorance
of barbarism for courage.

497
00:52:20,766 --> 00:52:22,205
What a pity...

498
00:52:23,726 --> 00:52:25,845
If I want to..

499
00:52:26,846 --> 00:52:31,645
...I can put my hand inside your
chest and take your heart out.

500
00:52:39,806 --> 00:52:41,485
But I don't want to do that.

501
00:52:44,286 --> 00:52:45,245
Why?

502
00:52:47,126 --> 00:52:50,485
First, your cities that you
love so much will burn.

503
00:52:50,926 --> 00:52:53,205
In flames.

504
00:52:53,206 --> 00:52:57,205
While they burn, your
people will scream and shout.

505
00:52:58,006 --> 00:53:00,525
You will see this first.

506
00:53:01,606 --> 00:53:03,445
You will be afraid.

507
00:53:05,526 --> 00:53:07,445
Then you will die.

508
00:53:20,806 --> 00:53:22,525
Tell me..

509
00:53:26,566 --> 00:53:29,165
What does Osman want from me?

510
00:53:29,806 --> 00:53:31,685
Osman Bey...

511
00:53:32,646 --> 00:53:35,085
...wants to meet with you...

512
00:53:35,806 --> 00:53:39,165
...tomorrow in the Akcapinar
to make an agreement.

513
00:53:40,246 --> 00:53:41,845
An agreement?

514
00:53:43,446 --> 00:53:45,325
War is coming.

515
00:53:45,886 --> 00:53:48,005
Osman will die anyway.

516
00:53:49,006 --> 00:53:51,485
Why would I agree?

517
00:53:57,526 --> 00:54:03,205
How do you know that fate won't bring
new victory to the Turks, Commander?

518
00:54:07,166 --> 00:54:11,045
My Osman Bey wants to make a
beneficial agreement for everyone.

519
00:54:22,766 --> 00:54:24,885
Tell Osman I will come.

520
00:54:36,326 --> 00:54:39,605
Let's meet then, Osman Bey.

521
00:54:41,126 --> 00:54:45,525
Let's meet.

522
00:54:45,526 --> 00:54:46,205
My Bey.

523
00:54:46,566 --> 00:54:50,565
What are we going to discuss? She
is a traitor. Isn't her punishment death?

524
00:54:50,566 --> 00:54:51,525
My Osman Bey.

525
00:54:52,286 --> 00:54:53,845
Forgive me.

526
00:54:53,846 --> 00:54:56,245
I made a mistake because of my anger and pride.

527
00:54:56,246 --> 00:54:58,005
Forgive me, my Bey.

528
00:54:58,526 --> 00:55:00,525
Anger and pride, huh?

529
00:55:00,766 --> 00:55:05,205
You united with the enemy,
Begum. You tried to hurt my children.

530
00:55:05,206 --> 00:55:08,005
I am saying that I regret it, Bala Hatun.

531
00:55:08,206 --> 00:55:12,685
I know there's no forgiveness for
what I did. But please show mercy.

532
00:55:13,366 --> 00:55:15,125
Osman Bey.

533
00:55:17,086 --> 00:55:19,885
Did you never think before betraying us?

534
00:55:23,086 --> 00:55:26,765
But the fear of death.

535
00:55:26,766 --> 00:55:28,645
When it comes...

536
00:55:28,646 --> 00:55:31,525
My eyes were blind to the truth, my Bey.

537
00:55:31,526 --> 00:55:35,205
Your brother

538
00:55:35,206 --> 00:55:37,125
What about your brother?

539
00:55:37,326 --> 00:55:39,845
He fought bravely and became a martyr.

540
00:55:39,846 --> 00:55:43,805
Allow me. Allow me to make up for it, my Bey.

541
00:55:43,886 --> 00:55:46,925
Let me die in a way that
befits my brother and my name.

542
00:55:46,926 --> 00:55:49,525
You didn't come here
after feeling regret, Begum.

543
00:55:49,526 --> 00:55:53,165
You were caught while you were making a
treacherous move. Don't you have shame?

544
00:55:53,166 --> 00:55:55,685
I don't want to die, Bala Hatun.

545
00:55:57,246 --> 00:55:59,245
I will do whatever you say.

546
00:56:08,086 --> 00:56:09,485
So...

547
00:56:10,246 --> 00:56:12,525
...you will do whatever we want, huh?

548
00:56:14,126 --> 00:56:18,845
Whatever you want, my Bey. Just don't kill me.

549
00:56:25,326 --> 00:56:28,325
I will give you a chance to save your life.

550
00:56:32,606 --> 00:56:35,405
Listen to me carefully.

551
00:57:08,206 --> 00:57:12,085
You came to see my dead body. But I am not dead.

552
00:57:12,086 --> 00:57:16,725
Shut up. My father must have a plan about you.

553
00:57:17,206 --> 00:57:23,085
Don't get happy, Begum. As long as you have
this greed, you will make more mistakes.

554
00:57:23,086 --> 00:57:27,645
And then, we will take
your life without hesitation.

555
00:57:27,806 --> 00:57:31,765
I have learned my lesson,
Hatuns. I won't make mistakes.

556
00:57:33,326 --> 00:57:36,925
We will see. From now on,
we will always be watching you.

557
00:57:38,926 --> 00:57:40,685
Look at this little traitor.

558
00:57:40,766 --> 00:57:43,805
What did you say? Shut up.

559
00:57:43,806 --> 00:57:47,045
Who do you call a traitor?
Don't make me kill you here!

560
00:57:47,046 --> 00:57:50,005
Fatma. Fatma.

561
00:57:57,206 --> 00:57:58,925
We are leaving.

562
00:58:13,126 --> 00:58:16,205
I might be mad, but we are family.

563
00:58:16,846 --> 00:58:18,525
Don't look at me like that.

564
00:58:27,926 --> 00:58:30,205
What am I going to do now?

565
00:59:29,726 --> 00:59:33,165
O the Owner of the skies and the earth.

566
00:59:33,406 --> 00:59:35,605
O my Allah, the Most Glorious.

567
00:59:35,606 --> 00:59:38,325
The most Merciful of the merciful.

568
00:59:38,326 --> 00:59:39,845
My Allah..

569
00:59:39,886 --> 00:59:43,685
May You forgive all my sins, past and present.

570
00:59:43,686 --> 00:59:47,365
Do not separate me from the
path of the Prophets, my Allah.

571
00:59:47,686 --> 00:59:50,485
O my Allah, the Most Glorious.

572
00:59:50,486 --> 00:59:53,085
Do not withhold Your help from us.

573
00:59:53,086 --> 00:59:57,125
Make every step we take for Your cause firm.

574
00:59:57,126 --> 01:00:01,445
May You give strength to my
state, my people, and my army.

575
01:00:01,526 --> 01:00:07,165
Do not separate me and my descendants
from Your cause and Your path, my Allah.

576
01:00:07,166 --> 01:00:11,565
May You grant us victory over our enemies.

577
01:00:11,606 --> 01:00:13,925
Aameen.

578
01:00:25,086 --> 01:00:27,165
Can I come in, my Bey?

579
01:00:27,326 --> 01:00:29,085
Come in Boran.

580
01:00:32,046 --> 01:00:36,085
My Bey, Claudius has agreed to meet.

581
01:00:36,086 --> 01:00:38,885
Alright then. Make the preparations.

582
01:00:38,886 --> 01:00:40,565
As you order my Bey.

583
01:00:46,806 --> 01:00:47,965
Bala.

584
01:00:47,966 --> 01:00:49,325
My Bey.

585
01:00:49,926 --> 01:00:52,365
Claudius accepted the meeting.

586
01:00:54,086 --> 01:00:57,365
We sent Begum with Aykurt before the sunrise.

587
01:00:57,886 --> 01:00:59,405
I didn't take her life.

588
01:00:59,446 --> 01:01:03,445
For our state, her living self is
more valuable than her dead body.

589
01:01:23,846 --> 01:01:28,285
My father Koca Bey did the right thing by
pledging allegiance to Osman Bey, uncle.

590
01:01:28,926 --> 01:01:32,846
The valiants who'll be raised here, 
the Ergenekon of Turks...

591
01:01:32,846 --> 01:01:36,166
...will strike the enemy's chest like a ram.

592
01:01:36,166 --> 01:01:41,285
The man holds the sword,
the Bey says the word, Oguz.

593
01:01:42,086 --> 01:01:46,485
I fear that these glorious valiants
will die under Osman's command.

594
01:01:47,566 --> 01:01:50,725
Uncle, what do you mean?

595
01:01:50,766 --> 01:01:57,045
Having the state which settled in
the hearts of Turks is our right, Oguz.

596
01:02:04,166 --> 01:02:06,085
Ah uncle..

597
01:02:06,366 --> 01:02:10,085
I hope my father does not
hear these words of yours.

598
01:02:12,846 --> 01:02:17,685
It was my grandmother's heirloom. It should
be somewhere around here. Let's find it.

599
01:02:28,526 --> 01:02:30,805
Is this yours, Kayi girl?

600
01:02:31,366 --> 01:02:33,005
Why do you have it?

601
01:02:33,006 --> 01:02:35,885
I don't know. You tell me.

602
01:02:40,646 --> 01:02:41,885
Give it to me.

603
01:02:41,886 --> 01:02:44,605
Are Kayi girls always this angry?

604
01:02:44,806 --> 01:02:48,725
Angry? Who are you for
me to get angry at you, huh?

605
01:02:48,726 --> 01:02:50,885
I said give it to me, or else...

606
01:02:52,646 --> 01:02:54,325
Or else what?

607
01:02:58,846 --> 01:03:02,245
Is this the reward for my favor, Kayi girl?

608
01:03:02,646 --> 01:03:06,165
Favor? I am the one who is doing you a favor.

609
01:03:06,166 --> 01:03:09,005
Despite your madness,
I can still control myself.

610
01:03:09,006 --> 01:03:12,725
Don't make me hurt you here. Go now.

611
01:03:31,446 --> 01:03:34,005
Who is he? Do you know him?

612
01:03:35,006 --> 01:03:36,765
I don't need to know him.

613
01:03:36,926 --> 01:03:40,045
Considering he dared to talk to me like that,

614
01:03:41,286 --> 01:03:43,005
...he must be a madman.

615
01:03:44,526 --> 01:03:46,605
A madman who lost his mind.

616
01:03:46,886 --> 01:03:50,405
Maybe, he lost his mind when he saw you.

617
01:03:52,046 --> 01:03:53,525
Halime.

618
01:03:53,886 --> 01:03:56,085
I say what I see, Fatma Hatun.

619
01:03:56,646 --> 01:03:57,885
Move.

620
01:04:11,766 --> 01:04:14,285
Osman Bey is up to something again.

621
01:04:14,966 --> 01:04:16,645
We'll see.

622
01:04:18,566 --> 01:04:22,205
In the name of Allah, the most
merciful, the most compassionate.

623
01:04:23,686 --> 01:04:26,365
-Brother.
-Father.

624
01:04:28,286 --> 01:04:29,725
My boy.

625
01:04:31,606 --> 01:04:35,045
My nephew wanted to come
immediately when you called us, brother.

626
01:04:35,046 --> 01:04:37,445
Turks are struggling for
their existence, my Bey.

627
01:04:37,446 --> 01:04:39,765
I wanted to join you during this tough fight.

628
01:04:39,846 --> 01:04:44,845
Well thought, my boy. We need
every man in this tough fight.

629
01:04:46,526 --> 01:04:51,005
What is the preparation
in the tribe for, my brother?

630
01:04:51,246 --> 01:04:54,365
Does it have anything to
do with you inviting me here?

631
01:04:54,366 --> 01:04:58,205
Tell the alps to be ready, Yigit.

632
01:04:58,646 --> 01:05:01,085
Why? A fight?

633
01:05:03,006 --> 01:05:04,365
Against whom?

634
01:05:05,366 --> 01:05:06,445
Wait.

635
01:05:07,086 --> 01:05:09,085
We'll talk after the council.

636
01:05:14,166 --> 01:05:15,765
After the council.

637
01:05:16,886 --> 01:05:20,525
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too.

638
01:05:21,446 --> 01:05:24,445
Ertugrul Ghazi's brave fellow.

639
01:05:25,486 --> 01:05:27,565
We've heard your name a lot.

640
01:05:31,446 --> 01:05:33,165
Welcome.

641
01:05:35,526 --> 01:05:38,885
Thank you, Koca Bey. Live long.

642
01:05:45,926 --> 01:05:48,085
Attention, Osman Bey!

643
01:05:51,766 --> 01:05:54,565
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too.

644
01:05:54,726 --> 01:05:56,405
Peace be upon you too.

645
01:06:05,246 --> 01:06:06,925
I invited you.

646
01:06:07,166 --> 01:06:10,285
And you came quickly. Thank you.

647
01:06:13,126 --> 01:06:16,565
The council which is being held here today...

648
01:06:16,646 --> 01:06:21,645
...will determine the
fate of Kayi and all Turks.

649
01:06:23,246 --> 01:06:24,765
As you know

650
01:06:25,446 --> 01:06:30,765
...the order and balance in the
frontiers keep changing all the time.

651
01:06:31,366 --> 01:06:38,285
Yet we, who follow the right
path, will bring the true order.

652
01:06:39,086 --> 01:06:44,325
They say the heathen emperor
gave you a cart of gold, Osman Bey.

653
01:06:44,646 --> 01:06:46,325
We've all heard that.

654
01:06:46,566 --> 01:06:50,005
Those men do nothing but evil.

655
01:06:50,046 --> 01:06:54,525
What order do they want to bring now?

656
01:06:54,646 --> 01:06:58,205
We didn't take only the
gold but also their castle.

657
01:07:04,686 --> 01:07:08,165
According to the deal between
me and Emperor Andronikos,

658
01:07:09,246 --> 01:07:13,245
...with no bloodshed and no martyrs,

659
01:07:15,166 --> 01:07:19,565
...we took the castle of Karacabes for Turks.

660
01:07:22,806 --> 01:07:24,885
Karacabes, huh?

661
01:07:25,526 --> 01:07:31,965
It's the most important castle which
opens the way to Bursa in the west.

662
01:07:32,206 --> 01:07:33,565
Yes, the most important.

663
01:07:33,806 --> 01:07:38,325
For this reason, the order in Karacabes
should be maintained in no time.

664
01:07:38,846 --> 01:07:40,125
Well..

665
01:07:40,286 --> 01:07:43,885
If Claudius thinks that it's
going to be threat against Bursa...

666
01:07:46,086 --> 01:07:49,205
...when he learns that we captured the castle

667
01:07:52,686 --> 01:07:55,445
...he will certainly attempt
to make a move against us.

668
01:07:56,686 --> 01:08:03,045
The duty of ruling and reinforcing Karacabes...

669
01:08:05,806 --> 01:08:07,525
...is yours, Orhan Bey.

670
01:08:08,726 --> 01:08:11,165
Cerkutay has gone to take over the castle.

671
01:08:11,406 --> 01:08:16,885
From now on, you will live there with your wife.

672
01:08:17,886 --> 01:08:19,444
As you order, my Bey.

673
01:08:20,366 --> 01:08:23,205
Excuse me, my Bey. I
should go make preparations.

674
01:08:23,406 --> 01:08:25,245
Of course, of course.

675
01:08:31,246 --> 01:08:37,845
The heathens gave us the gift of
Karacabes in return for what, my Bey?

676
01:08:38,286 --> 01:08:40,245
I don't understand.

677
01:08:40,406 --> 01:08:46,365
Stopping the Mongolian army
while they come to our lands...

678
01:08:46,805 --> 01:08:51,205
...is an inevitable fight to protect our state.

679
01:08:52,046 --> 01:08:54,645
But there is one thing the emperor doesn't know.

680
01:08:55,366 --> 01:09:00,965
With the gold he gave us,
we will divide our enemies.

681
01:09:14,366 --> 01:09:18,045
Do you know what this letter means?

682
01:09:23,725 --> 01:09:26,444
You don't.

683
01:09:27,486 --> 01:09:33,045
This letter means you will..

684
01:09:35,366 --> 01:09:38,125
...surrender this castle...

685
01:09:39,446 --> 01:09:41,845
...unconditionally without a resistance.

686
01:09:49,246 --> 01:09:50,845
Alps!

687
01:09:51,845 --> 01:09:54,085
Show these soldiers the door.

688
01:09:54,206 --> 01:09:56,845
And make sure that they have all left.

689
01:09:57,046 --> 01:09:58,525
Come on.

690
01:10:01,566 --> 01:10:03,565
Put those rags down.

691
01:10:03,766 --> 01:10:07,485
Hang our glorious banners instead.

692
01:10:08,166 --> 01:10:14,325
The whole world should know
that Osman Bey took this castle...

693
01:10:14,646 --> 01:10:17,165
...without swords but with politics.

694
01:10:18,406 --> 01:10:25,245
With the gold the emperor gave you,
you'll both make Claudius be your ally...

695
01:10:25,566 --> 01:10:28,325
...and separate him from Kucar...

696
01:10:28,526 --> 01:10:33,245
...and make him leave his nest with the news...

697
01:10:33,606 --> 01:10:35,365
..and take his head.

698
01:10:35,566 --> 01:10:37,285
Is that right, my Bey?

699
01:10:38,926 --> 01:10:41,885
They will think we are making a mistake.

700
01:10:43,406 --> 01:10:46,605
But it will be them who
makes the biggest mistake.

701
01:10:47,766 --> 01:10:49,525
What about the Mongolian army?

702
01:10:49,926 --> 01:10:52,725
They're marching from the
east to the west sneakily.

703
01:10:55,446 --> 01:10:57,445
What is our target?

704
01:11:13,926 --> 01:11:16,365
According to the information we got.

705
01:11:17,326 --> 01:11:22,125
...the Mongolian army will pass
through here and come to our borders.

706
01:11:23,286 --> 01:11:27,285
We don't know which route they will follow next.

707
01:11:27,606 --> 01:11:31,645
But we'll put them in the route we want.

708
01:11:31,846 --> 01:11:34,525
How will that be possible, my Bey?

709
01:11:36,406 --> 01:11:38,525
An army can march with no food.

710
01:11:39,006 --> 01:11:41,645
But without water, they can't walk.

711
01:11:43,246 --> 01:11:48,405
For this reason, we will make all
the water wells in this area unusable.

712
01:11:49,166 --> 01:11:55,285
We'll only leave this area available for them.

713
01:11:57,126 --> 01:11:59,925
-Camlica region, my Bey.
-Camlica region.

714
01:12:00,366 --> 01:12:04,685
Streams and the cliffs there.
They will pass through them.

715
01:12:05,086 --> 01:12:09,125
And they will fall into our trap.

716
01:12:09,566 --> 01:12:12,125
Brilliant idea.

717
01:12:14,286 --> 01:12:16,605
They aren't our equals, but...

718
01:12:17,486 --> 01:12:20,645
...we and the heathens
are in equal conditions now.

719
01:12:24,286 --> 01:12:26,325
I'm ready for this mission.

720
01:12:27,926 --> 01:12:29,565
Okay, okay.

721
01:12:31,646 --> 01:12:32,925
Well..

722
01:12:34,846 --> 01:12:36,525
Turgut Ghazi.

723
01:12:37,086 --> 01:12:38,565
-Alaaddin.
-My Bey.

724
01:12:38,806 --> 01:12:39,925
And Turahan.

725
01:12:42,006 --> 01:12:45,365
It's your duty to break Mongolians.

726
01:12:45,566 --> 01:12:48,045
-As you order, my Bey.
-As you order, my Bey.

727
01:12:48,526 --> 01:12:49,925
Okay.

728
01:12:51,846 --> 01:12:53,725
And you, Turahan.

729
01:12:57,446 --> 01:13:05,205
You won't let even a single
soldier come from the east.

730
01:13:05,686 --> 01:13:07,925
With the alps you take

731
01:13:08,726 --> 01:13:10,565
...this duty is yours.

732
01:13:13,726 --> 01:13:18,285
You'll be the border commander of the frontiers.

733
01:13:18,566 --> 01:13:22,045
I'd sacrifice my life for Islam, my Bey.

734
01:13:22,526 --> 01:13:27,165
I swear I will carry out this
duty with my life and blood.

735
01:13:27,566 --> 01:13:29,965
Thank you, thank you.

736
01:13:32,646 --> 01:13:35,165
Turgut Ghazi, my father's fellow.

737
01:13:36,926 --> 01:13:39,685
You beat my alps during the training, huh?

738
01:13:42,606 --> 01:13:44,645
Your alps are well trained.

739
01:13:45,446 --> 01:13:48,165
But we need to train the young ones.

740
01:13:49,286 --> 01:13:53,845
I want you to train the alps.

741
01:13:56,366 --> 01:14:00,565
You have trained many men
and broken many bones, huh?

742
01:14:01,206 --> 01:14:02,885
Your wish is my command.

743
01:14:04,766 --> 01:14:06,605
I'll carry out the duty.

744
01:14:06,766 --> 01:14:08,485
Thank you, thank you.

745
01:14:09,526 --> 01:14:10,765
Here we go.

746
01:14:11,366 --> 01:14:13,445
Everybody knows their duties.

747
01:14:16,166 --> 01:14:18,045
It's time for fight.

748
01:14:18,126 --> 01:14:20,365
Yes, my Bey!

749
01:14:37,766 --> 01:14:40,245
What decision did the council give, brother?

750
01:14:40,326 --> 01:14:43,325
Against whom will we send all those alps?

751
01:14:44,046 --> 01:14:49,925
Kucar, Orlok of Mongolians, who dishonors
the frontiers with every step he takes.

752
01:14:51,326 --> 01:14:55,685
We'll march towards that dog's
armies marching to the frontiers.

753
01:14:56,886 --> 01:15:00,725
We'll beat and destroy
all of them, with Allah's will.

754
01:15:07,926 --> 01:15:10,525
You'll stay here, Oghuz.

755
01:15:11,126 --> 01:15:14,565
They need Beys and soldiers here too, right?

756
01:15:15,806 --> 01:15:18,485
My brave son!

757
01:15:21,606 --> 01:15:23,285
Osman Bey.

758
01:15:25,006 --> 01:15:26,805
He's going to beat Kucar, huh?

759
01:15:27,206 --> 01:15:29,645
Attention, Osman Bey!

760
01:15:43,406 --> 01:15:45,485
O people!

761
01:15:46,126 --> 01:15:48,965
My Beys! My alps!

762
01:15:50,726 --> 01:15:56,165
You, who sacrificed a lot for the sake
of Allah and for the glory of our state!

763
01:15:57,446 --> 01:15:59,245
The council is over.

764
01:16:00,006 --> 01:16:03,405
Now it's time for fight.

765
01:16:03,486 --> 01:16:08,445
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

766
01:16:09,206 --> 01:16:13,085
Some betrayed us.

767
01:16:14,206 --> 01:16:18,125
Some brought troubles from distant places!

768
01:16:19,086 --> 01:16:25,365
But they all intended to
capture and destroy Turks.

769
01:16:27,246 --> 01:16:28,965
I'm asking you.

770
01:16:30,046 --> 01:16:31,885
Will we let that happen?

771
01:16:32,006 --> 01:16:36,565
Never! Never, my Bey!

772
01:16:36,846 --> 01:16:38,565
Of course not.

773
01:16:38,966 --> 01:16:40,445
Of course not.

774
01:16:40,646 --> 01:16:47,405
Those fools are reaching out to
harm our existence and freedom!

775
01:16:50,326 --> 01:16:54,605
Well... The warriors of the Prophet's.

776
01:16:55,846 --> 01:16:58,005
Brave fighters!

777
01:16:59,446 --> 01:17:03,845
Don't get your heads down
because we are outnumbered!

778
01:17:04,846 --> 01:17:09,045
Don't encourage the ones
who are happy to outnumber us!

779
01:17:09,766 --> 01:17:12,045
Our faith melting the iron mountains...

780
01:17:12,686 --> 01:17:14,805
...will destroy all of them!

781
01:17:25,046 --> 01:17:28,645
This sword is a weapon to them.

782
01:17:29,846 --> 01:17:32,165
But it's a brother to us.

783
01:17:33,206 --> 01:17:38,045
Death scaring them is a fabulous feast to us!

784
01:17:38,406 --> 01:17:42,045
They can't be martyrs or ghazis. Only we can!

785
01:17:42,966 --> 01:17:48,245
What will make us victorious is
the blood shed for the sake of Allah!

786
01:17:48,846 --> 01:17:49,925
Allah is the greatest!

787
01:17:50,046 --> 01:17:53,725
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!

788
01:17:53,806 --> 01:17:56,365
-Allah is the greatest!
-Allah is the greatest!

789
01:18:11,206 --> 01:18:16,365
I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed satan

790
01:18:17,406 --> 01:18:22,765
In the name of Allah,
the most compassionate, the most merciful.

791
01:18:23,926 --> 01:18:29,930
Truly We have opened up a path to 
clear triumph for you [Prophet],

792
01:18:30,606 --> 01:18:38,856
so that God may forgive you
your past and future sins

793
01:18:39,766 --> 01:18:47,696
complete His grace upon you,
guide you to a straight path,

794
01:18:47,696 --> 01:18:54,395
and help you mightily.

795
01:18:54,862 --> 01:19:06,165
It was He who made His tranquillity 
descend into the hearts of the believers

796
01:19:06,287 --> 01:19:13,085
o add faith to their faith, the forces 
of the heavens and earth belong to God;

797
01:19:13,526 --> 01:19:19,845
He is all knowing and all wise

798
01:19:19,904 --> 01:19:29,893
so as to admit believing men and women into
Gardens graced with flowing streams

799
01:19:29,893 --> 01:19:36,892
there to remain, absolving their bad deeds

800
01:19:36,892 --> 01:19:43,674
a great triumph in God’s eyes

801
01:19:43,764 --> 01:20:00,029
and to torment the hypocritical and idolatrous men
and women who harbour evil thoughts about God

802
01:20:00,029 --> 01:20:09,068
it is they who will be encircled by evil!

803
01:20:09,068 --> 01:20:17,216
who carry the burden of God’s anger

804
01:20:17,216 --> 01:20:32,241
whom God has rejected and for whom 
He has prepared Hell, an evil destination!

805
01:20:32,241 --> 01:20:40,253
The forces of heaven and earth belong to God;

806
01:20:40,253 --> 01:20:46,788
He is almighty and all wise.

807
01:20:46,788 --> 01:20:55,976
We have sent you [Prophet] to bring
good news and to give warning,

808
01:20:55,976 --> 01:21:01,296
so that you[people] may believe in God and His Messenger

809
01:21:01,296 --> 01:21:10,595
support Him, honour Him, and praise Him morning and evening.

810
01:21:21,206 --> 01:21:23,605
Will we trust Osman, sir?

811
01:21:25,886 --> 01:21:28,565
I trust nobody but myself.

812
01:21:29,406 --> 01:21:32,405
Wait in the woods with your best men.

813
01:21:34,446 --> 01:21:37,285
Come here. Come.

814
01:21:47,406 --> 01:21:52,285
Osman... Let's see what you
will promise to convince me.

815
01:22:09,446 --> 01:22:11,525
Our army will come soon.

816
01:22:11,526 --> 01:22:15,405
What will Osman's first move be, Kucar?

817
01:22:15,646 --> 01:22:18,765
Osman will surely make a move.

818
01:22:18,766 --> 01:22:22,125
He doesn't know where our army is but...

819
01:22:25,806 --> 01:22:31,085
...he will poison all the wells on the border.

820
01:22:31,086 --> 01:22:36,125
Osman will not risk the innocent
people's lives by doing this.

821
01:22:37,966 --> 01:22:41,165
He will find a solution for that.

822
01:22:41,166 --> 01:22:43,605
We need to make a move to prevent this.

823
01:22:44,046 --> 01:22:46,085
We already did.

824
01:22:47,686 --> 01:22:53,005
No one will drink water
before taking precautions.

825
01:22:53,006 --> 01:22:57,205
If the wells are poisoned, our army...

826
01:22:57,206 --> 01:23:05,205
...will come through the valleys
from Camlica, between the streams.

827
01:23:05,686 --> 01:23:10,165
This way, they will both
be able to drink water...

828
01:23:10,286 --> 01:23:15,005
...and move forward without being noticed.

829
01:23:19,086 --> 01:23:26,845
This is such poison that even a
single drop will destroy a person.

830
01:23:30,286 --> 01:23:33,725
In the name of Allah,
the most merciful, the most compassionate.

831
01:23:36,686 --> 01:23:41,365
They will either control
the wells or drink and die.

832
01:23:42,006 --> 01:23:44,805
Both paths lead to our victory.

833
01:23:45,406 --> 01:23:47,725
If they notice the poison...

834
01:23:49,526 --> 01:23:52,485
...they will turn their way towards the Camlica.

835
01:23:52,486 --> 01:23:54,685
Now we will wait.

836
01:23:55,446 --> 01:24:00,845
They will die either by poison or by the sword.

837
01:24:01,166 --> 01:24:04,645
We will send them away like
sending dogs away, my Shahzade.

838
01:24:05,286 --> 01:24:11,045
The cost of invading our lands is
bleeding to death. Everyone will see.

839
01:24:11,966 --> 01:24:13,645
They will.

840
01:24:13,646 --> 01:24:19,365
Alps, poison all the wells, troughs,
and water bodies in the area.

841
01:24:19,366 --> 01:24:21,045
Lay in ambush.

842
01:24:21,566 --> 01:24:26,285
Do not let the people approach the
places you have poisoned for a while. Go!

843
01:24:31,286 --> 01:24:32,925
Come on.

844
01:25:09,166 --> 01:25:11,885
Come, Hatun, come.

845
01:25:11,886 --> 01:25:13,925
Share my food with me.

846
01:25:13,926 --> 01:25:15,285
Take this.

847
01:25:15,286 --> 01:25:16,645
Eat it.

848
01:25:16,686 --> 01:25:18,765
Thank you Kucar.

849
01:25:19,446 --> 01:25:22,285
I brought you important news.

850
01:25:23,886 --> 01:25:25,445
Tell me.

851
01:25:25,446 --> 01:25:28,045
My spy in the tribe heard it.

852
01:25:28,126 --> 01:25:30,725
That Claudius that you trust so much...

853
01:25:30,726 --> 01:25:32,845
...is allies with Osman.

854
01:25:32,846 --> 01:25:35,565
What are you saying, Hatun?

855
01:25:35,966 --> 01:25:39,405
They are going to meet in Akcapinar.

856
01:25:39,886 --> 01:25:44,125
It is time to cut the heads of these two devils.

857
01:25:44,126 --> 01:25:46,085
Mankurt.

858
01:25:46,726 --> 01:25:50,965
Go and check if this
Hatun is telling the truth!

859
01:25:51,046 --> 01:25:54,245
I'll come after you! Go!

860
01:25:54,726 --> 01:25:56,965
You wait, Hatun.

861
01:25:59,166 --> 01:26:05,885
...you are not telling me the
truth, I will skin you Hatun!

862
01:26:22,646 --> 01:26:24,725
That demon is walking around.

863
01:26:24,726 --> 01:26:26,845
And he got really mad.

864
01:26:43,366 --> 01:26:45,525
It is the order of my Osman Bey.

865
01:26:45,526 --> 01:26:49,605
If you are playing a game, I will
kill you here with my own hands.

866
01:26:49,606 --> 01:26:52,205
Why would I come with you
if I wanted to play a game?

867
01:26:52,206 --> 01:26:54,245
I am just warning you.

868
01:27:01,886 --> 01:27:05,445
Alps, we are returning to the tribe. Come on!

869
01:27:21,006 --> 01:27:23,925
Those are Mongol scouts, my Shahzade.

870
01:27:29,486 --> 01:27:31,405
Draw water from the well!

871
01:27:36,926 --> 01:27:39,365
They took the bait!

872
01:27:39,406 --> 01:27:41,885
They will give that water to their horses...

873
01:27:41,886 --> 01:27:45,445
But the horses won't drink that
water. They will sense the poison.

874
01:27:45,766 --> 01:27:48,405
Two heads are better than one, my Shahzade.

875
01:27:48,406 --> 01:27:52,205
They will escape from the
poison but get caught by the sword.

876
01:27:52,526 --> 01:27:54,485
God willing. God willing.

877
01:28:12,526 --> 01:28:14,405
Orlok Kucar is right.

878
01:28:14,406 --> 01:28:15,925
The water is poisoned.

879
01:28:15,926 --> 01:28:19,125
We will inform the Commander
of the army. Come on!

880
01:28:34,806 --> 01:28:38,845
There is no way for them to pass
through here to reach the water channels.

881
01:28:38,846 --> 01:28:44,085
They will fall into our trap... Then...

882
01:28:44,206 --> 01:28:47,125
...the soil will be watered with Mongol blood.

883
01:29:27,766 --> 01:29:29,445
Wait here.

884
01:29:31,766 --> 01:29:33,245
Osman.

885
01:29:34,046 --> 01:29:35,645
What happened?

886
01:29:35,966 --> 01:29:39,005
Did we come here to
celebrate my victory in Bursa?

887
01:29:39,086 --> 01:29:42,565
I came to remove those chains from your neck.

888
01:29:42,646 --> 01:29:44,165
Chains?

889
01:29:44,806 --> 01:29:49,125
I guess I came here to listen to
your ridiculous words, is that it?

890
01:29:50,406 --> 01:29:53,085
I am talking about the chains on your neck.

891
01:29:54,926 --> 01:29:59,205
The chain Kucar put around your neck.

892
01:30:04,886 --> 01:30:08,005
Now you're really starting to talk nonsense.

893
01:30:09,286 --> 01:30:14,045
-You know we're talking about my ally, right?
-He's not your ally.

894
01:30:14,486 --> 01:30:16,525
Kucar is your owner.

895
01:30:18,886 --> 01:30:21,325
And we both know that.

896
01:30:26,766 --> 01:30:28,365
Now..

897
01:30:28,446 --> 01:30:30,725
if you want Bursa...

898
01:30:31,006 --> 01:30:33,805
...you have to get rid of Kucar.

899
01:30:36,926 --> 01:30:39,725
You said we would fight against Kucar, brother.

900
01:30:40,966 --> 01:30:44,645
What is Osman Bey doing with that infidel now?

901
01:30:46,126 --> 01:30:49,556
His intention is to set the
dogs against each other,

902
01:30:49,568 --> 01:30:52,685
divide his enemies, and
swallow them one by one.

903
01:30:55,366 --> 01:30:56,685
Then..

904
01:30:56,846 --> 01:30:59,605
...how are we going to get rid of Kucar?

905
01:31:07,246 --> 01:31:08,765
Osman..

906
01:31:12,366 --> 01:31:15,285
I asked you. How are we
going to get rid of Kucar?

907
01:31:18,846 --> 01:31:20,125
Come on!

908
01:31:59,246 --> 01:32:00,845
What are you going to do?

909
01:32:00,846 --> 01:32:04,885
Will you give this gold and
tell Kucar to leave Bursa?

910
01:32:05,286 --> 01:32:10,565
This is your share of the gold.

911
01:32:12,606 --> 01:32:16,845
I mean... Your price.

912
01:32:16,926 --> 01:32:18,365
Price?

913
01:32:20,886 --> 01:32:23,445
While I am fighting with Kucar...

914
01:32:26,526 --> 01:32:28,765
...you won't join a side.

915
01:32:34,766 --> 01:32:38,765
I will rip him and his army out of these lands.

916
01:32:38,766 --> 01:32:40,245
And you..

917
01:32:41,366 --> 01:32:44,525
...will be the only ruler of Bursa.

918
01:32:46,646 --> 01:32:49,125
Well, well

919
01:32:50,126 --> 01:32:54,325
I always said that you are a smart man Osman.

920
01:32:56,406 --> 01:32:58,365
What's going to happen now?

921
01:32:58,686 --> 01:33:01,165
You will keep me away from this fight.

922
01:33:01,206 --> 01:33:05,045
You will win a victory against
Kucar without any losses.

923
01:33:08,926 --> 01:33:10,765
Then what will happen?

924
01:33:11,366 --> 01:33:13,165
Who's next?

925
01:33:14,006 --> 01:33:15,365
Me?

926
01:33:18,486 --> 01:33:20,965
This won't be a battle without losses.

927
01:33:22,526 --> 01:33:24,605
We will lose our men and get hurt.

928
01:33:25,726 --> 01:33:29,925
But I don't want to make a move while injured.

929
01:33:31,366 --> 01:33:34,685
I also don't want anyone
coming at me while I'm hurt.

930
01:33:37,646 --> 01:33:39,045
That s why

931
01:33:41,726 --> 01:33:43,405
...I want this gold...

932
01:33:44,766 --> 01:33:47,765
...to be the symbol of peace between us...

933
01:33:48,686 --> 01:33:51,885
...in the alliance we make against Kucar.

934
01:33:57,006 --> 01:33:58,445
Alright then.

935
01:33:59,286 --> 01:34:03,765
But our enmity remains. Right?

936
01:34:09,566 --> 01:34:14,765
Our enmity will last until one of us dies.

937
01:34:15,726 --> 01:34:17,205
Good

938
01:34:24,206 --> 01:34:29,205
Before killing Kucar, tell
him how much I sold him for.

939
01:34:29,686 --> 01:34:31,925
I don't want him to think he was cheap.

940
01:35:08,166 --> 01:35:10,685
What Begum said is true.

941
01:35:10,766 --> 01:35:15,925
Osman and Claudius made an
alliance. They will make peace and trade.

942
01:35:18,006 --> 01:35:20,245
Claudius..

943
01:35:21,206 --> 01:35:25,605
If I don't burn you in the flames...

944
01:35:26,086 --> 01:35:30,765
...may they not call me Kucar.

945
01:35:30,766 --> 01:35:35,885
Osman gave a cart full
of gold for this alliance.

946
01:35:35,886 --> 01:35:38,485
Their alliance is now definite.

947
01:35:39,086 --> 01:35:46,925
To teach everyone a lesson, I will
skin Claudius in the middle of Bursa.

948
01:35:49,286 --> 01:35:52,325
Let's go! Come on!

949
01:35:57,406 --> 01:36:00,005
We have put the Mongols on our path.

950
01:36:00,086 --> 01:36:02,445
Now, they will become our prey.

951
01:36:02,686 --> 01:36:06,285
And that fool Kucar is not with them.

952
01:36:06,806 --> 01:36:12,005
They will never come together
as well. Our plan worked.

953
01:36:17,286 --> 01:36:19,125
Osman Bey was right again.

954
01:36:19,126 --> 01:36:23,365
May Allah grant us another victory.
May He grant us another one, God willing.

955
01:36:23,366 --> 01:36:26,245
God willing.
God willing.

956
01:36:28,126 --> 01:36:31,885
I was destined to fight next to
my grandfather's companion.

957
01:36:32,326 --> 01:36:34,325
Thanks to my Allah..

958
01:36:35,846 --> 01:36:39,045
Thanks to my Allah, Alaeddin Ali. Thanks to Him.

959
01:36:40,486 --> 01:36:44,525
From now on, neither arrows nor
spears will be able to defeat me.

960
01:36:44,646 --> 01:36:47,268
Seeing that the family
of Ertugrul Bey, may his

961
01:36:47,280 --> 01:36:49,805
place be heaven, have
grown like a plane tree,

962
01:36:52,206 --> 01:36:54,445
...I'd die with pleasure.

963
01:36:56,206 --> 01:37:00,045
Just wait, Turgut Ghazi. Just wait, old man.

964
01:37:00,726 --> 01:37:05,245
There are many bones and walls to break.

965
01:37:06,246 --> 01:37:07,765
Alright.

966
01:37:08,246 --> 01:37:13,525
But now it's time to
slaughter those blood suckers!

967
01:37:17,126 --> 01:37:20,005
Come on. We need to go.

968
01:37:41,926 --> 01:37:44,005
Osman!

969
01:37:44,886 --> 01:37:46,245
Well..

970
01:37:47,886 --> 01:37:51,685
You will beg for mercy. I will take your life!

971
01:38:12,926 --> 01:38:20,005
I'd rather I could kill Claudius who
betrayed me by holding your hand, but...

972
01:38:20,486 --> 01:38:22,845
...I have to kill you first, Osman.

973
01:38:23,326 --> 01:38:25,685
Kill me? No.

974
01:38:26,006 --> 01:38:30,285
Who could even have a
more terrible fate than you?

975
01:38:35,046 --> 01:38:37,965
What unbreakable courage you have, Osman!

976
01:38:39,686 --> 01:38:44,445
You lost your tribe against a troop of nokers.

977
01:38:44,886 --> 01:38:47,725
You think you can win against my armies?

978
01:38:48,366 --> 01:38:50,485
You rely on your army?

979
01:38:50,726 --> 01:38:55,805
Tell me then. Where is your
army now? What are they doing?

980
01:39:00,966 --> 01:39:02,725
What are you talking about?

981
01:39:03,046 --> 01:39:04,365
Speak clearly.

982
01:39:04,646 --> 01:39:07,845
Shahzades you were trying to capture.

983
01:39:11,126 --> 01:39:14,805
They are busy destroying your army right now.

984
01:39:23,446 --> 01:39:28,045
And my part is killing a demon like you.

985
01:39:30,366 --> 01:39:34,205
You think you can destroy my armies?

986
01:39:34,806 --> 01:39:36,885
I'm not only ruining your armies...

987
01:39:36,966 --> 01:39:43,925
...but also all your plans against
my state, nation and family!

988
01:39:45,166 --> 01:39:47,485
Well... Today,

989
01:39:48,406 --> 01:39:51,525
...you're going deep under the ground.

990
01:40:51,206 --> 01:40:54,285
Archers, now!

991
01:40:55,926 --> 01:40:58,125
In the name of Allah.

992
01:41:30,926 --> 01:41:32,965
In the name of Allah.

993
01:42:14,686 --> 01:42:15,885
Come on, alps!

994
01:42:16,086 --> 01:42:19,965
Until nokers, who are our
enemies, die! Allah is the greatest!

995
01:42:20,046 --> 01:42:21,725
Allah is the greatest!

996
01:42:22,046 --> 01:42:24,925
-Come on, brothers!
-In the name of Allah!

997
01:42:47,486 --> 01:42:49,605
Allah is the greatest!

998
01:43:08,686 --> 01:43:10,685
Osman Bey's alps.

999
01:43:18,446 --> 01:43:20,325
Osman Bey was always right.

1000
01:43:20,566 --> 01:43:26,165
We made a mistake. Now it's
time to make up for our mistake.

1001
01:43:26,446 --> 01:43:28,525
Come on, come on!

1002
01:43:29,966 --> 01:43:31,405
Come on!

1003
01:43:32,526 --> 01:43:36,285
We're here for help, warriors! Allah is the greatest!

1004
01:43:47,486 --> 01:43:50,325
Thank you, valiant. You are
a great fighter, Praise be.

1005
01:43:50,406 --> 01:43:52,365
Thank you, Turgut Ghazi.

1006
01:44:21,566 --> 01:44:23,325
Come on, brothers!

1007
01:44:23,446 --> 01:44:26,325
Allah is the greatest!

1008
01:44:41,926 --> 01:44:43,525
The Righteous!

1009
01:44:50,126 --> 01:44:52,045
The Righteous!

1010
01:45:08,526 --> 01:45:11,165
I've seen many tongueless dogs like you.

1011
01:45:15,526 --> 01:45:20,445
I've always killed you with my sword of justice.

1012
01:45:24,966 --> 01:45:28,645
-Nokers!
-Here we go.

1013
01:46:08,646 --> 01:46:10,445
You heathen dog.

1014
01:46:41,126 --> 01:46:43,685
Where are you going?

1015
01:46:49,006 --> 01:46:51,765
I'm talking to you. Where are you going?

1016
01:46:52,366 --> 01:46:54,605
Look at me.

1017
01:47:01,526 --> 01:47:04,165
Your time is over, Kucar.

1018
01:47:11,926 --> 01:47:14,245
Your evil actions cannot be covered now.

1019
01:47:14,686 --> 01:47:16,765
You'll pay for what you did.

1020
01:48:19,166 --> 01:48:21,685
Allah is the greatest!

1021
01:48:45,606 --> 01:48:49,045
-Victory is ours!
-Allah is the greatest!

1022
01:48:49,166 --> 01:48:54,205
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!

1023
01:49:06,166 --> 01:49:07,645
Hasan Bey.

1024
01:49:07,966 --> 01:49:11,725
You had abandoned the tribe.

1025
01:49:12,526 --> 01:49:15,605
Tell me now. Why did you come for help?

1026
01:49:17,686 --> 01:49:20,045
I was blind. Alaaddin Bey.

1027
01:49:20,686 --> 01:49:22,485
I couldn't see the truth.

1028
01:49:23,606 --> 01:49:28,525
But then I realized that Osman
Bey's path was the straight path.

1029
01:49:30,126 --> 01:49:33,485
Many Beys and alps made the same mistake.

1030
01:49:34,206 --> 01:49:38,325
But realizing your mistake
is a virtue, Hasan Bey.

1031
01:49:38,646 --> 01:49:41,645
It is. It is but...

1032
01:49:42,406 --> 01:49:45,125
..I can't look at Osman Bey's face anymore.

1033
01:49:47,446 --> 01:49:50,645
Have a safe path. I will go my own way.

1034
01:49:59,206 --> 01:50:01,885
Oghuzs must be one body, boy.

1035
01:50:02,726 --> 01:50:06,445
If we get separated, we
will give the enemy a chance.

1036
01:50:07,406 --> 01:50:10,485
Obviously, Hasan Bey regrets what he did.

1037
01:50:14,446 --> 01:50:17,045
We should let Osman Bey know this.

1038
01:50:20,926 --> 01:50:23,925
I thought you were smart, Osman.

1039
01:50:24,406 --> 01:50:26,285
But you are a fool too.

1040
01:50:26,406 --> 01:50:30,805
You made a lot of mistakes
and are kneeling before me now.

1041
01:50:31,006 --> 01:50:34,165
You fell into my trap.

1042
01:50:35,566 --> 01:50:38,885
Trap? What are you talking about?

1043
01:50:40,286 --> 01:50:41,965
Claudius.

1044
01:50:42,206 --> 01:50:46,085
-The deal I made with Claudius.
-What are you talking about, Osman?

1045
01:50:46,526 --> 01:50:49,845
-Speak clearly!
-Who brought you the information?

1046
01:50:53,086 --> 01:50:54,805
Begum.

1047
01:50:56,806 --> 01:50:58,125
Yes, Begum.

1048
01:50:58,486 --> 01:51:00,245
Begum!

1049
01:51:00,566 --> 01:51:02,445
Begum, of course.

1050
01:51:03,006 --> 01:51:04,725
Have your never doubted?

1051
01:51:05,126 --> 01:51:09,965
You thought the one who betrayed
her state and nation wouldn't betray you?

1052
01:51:11,846 --> 01:51:15,965
In return for gold, I got your
deal with Claudius canceled.

1053
01:51:17,006 --> 01:51:21,085
And with the information,
you became a prey for me.

1054
01:51:23,606 --> 01:51:25,525
What about my armies?

1055
01:51:25,646 --> 01:51:26,925
How did you...

1056
01:51:27,006 --> 01:51:31,805
We didn't poison the
wells to kill your soldiers...

1057
01:51:32,086 --> 01:51:36,325
...but to make them go
near the river in despair.

1058
01:51:41,366 --> 01:51:47,605
You think you can overcome Mongolians...

1059
01:51:48,086 --> 01:51:53,525
...by killing me and breaking my
armies marching to the frontiers?

1060
01:51:53,886 --> 01:51:58,565
Every army you break and every life you take...

1061
01:51:59,006 --> 01:52:03,445
...will come back as a bigger trouble, Osman.

1062
01:52:03,646 --> 01:52:06,845
Come! You can all come!

1063
01:52:07,926 --> 01:52:09,045
Look at me.

1064
01:52:09,126 --> 01:52:11,205
Since I first saw you

1065
01:52:11,406 --> 01:52:14,445
...my sword has always been bloodthirsty.

1066
01:52:14,566 --> 01:52:16,485
It's time for you to die now.

1067
01:52:16,606 --> 01:52:19,765
Mongolians never bleed, Osman.

1068
01:52:20,246 --> 01:52:23,765
Mongolian soldiers flow like a flood.

1069
01:52:24,086 --> 01:52:28,125
And you will drown in that flood, Osman.

1070
01:52:29,326 --> 01:52:31,445
You say so?

1071
01:52:34,726 --> 01:52:37,925
If you are a flood, we become a dam.

1072
01:52:38,846 --> 01:52:41,965
If you are an avalanche, we become a mountain.

1073
01:52:43,166 --> 01:52:47,165
Whatever you

1074
01:52:47,846 --> 01:52:52,125
...we will always be against you.

1075
01:53:00,126 --> 01:53:01,805
Now...

1076
01:53:03,206 --> 01:53:06,165
Now your time is over.

1077
01:53:30,526 --> 01:53:34,525
I swear on my sword painted red with blood!

1078
01:53:34,606 --> 01:53:39,325
Whoever dishonors the right
religion Islam and the glory of Turks...

1079
01:53:39,606 --> 01:53:45,805
...will always lie on the
ground like this corpse!

1080
01:53:47,926 --> 01:53:50,925
Allah is the greatest!

1081
01:53:51,206 --> 01:53:57,205
-Allah is the greatest!
-Allah is the greatest!

1082
01:54:10,606 --> 01:54:13,125
Good.

1083
01:54:13,246 --> 01:54:16,125
Praise be, sisters. Praise be.

1084
01:54:16,126 --> 01:54:18,045
Our raids have restarted.

1085
01:54:18,526 --> 01:54:20,405
We have to be ready for duties.

1086
01:54:20,566 --> 01:54:22,205
Never stop training.

1087
01:54:22,286 --> 01:54:25,325
As you order, Bala Hatun!

1088
01:54:29,446 --> 01:54:31,485
It's your turn, Halime Hatun.

1089
01:54:31,686 --> 01:54:33,725
Show me your skills.

1090
01:54:35,086 --> 01:54:36,645
As you order, mother.

1091
01:55:15,646 --> 01:55:17,085
Praise be.

1092
01:55:17,286 --> 01:55:19,485
-You're good.
-Not at all, mother.

1093
01:55:19,766 --> 01:55:21,245
I dropped my sword.

1094
01:55:21,686 --> 01:55:24,925
You were fighting against
Bala Hatun, the head of Sisters.

1095
01:55:27,046 --> 01:55:30,125
I'm not like anyone else, dear.

1096
01:55:31,886 --> 01:55:35,485
Fatma, Halime should keep training with Sisters.

1097
01:55:36,086 --> 01:55:40,645
However agile she is, she must be trained by us.

1098
01:55:41,006 --> 01:55:43,005
Don't worry, mother.

1099
01:55:44,446 --> 01:55:46,885
I will trained her well.

1100
01:55:47,606 --> 01:55:49,405
-Bala Hatun.
-Come.

1101
01:55:51,286 --> 01:55:54,525
That snake woman insists on not eating anything.

1102
01:55:56,886 --> 01:55:59,325
-She has never left the tent.
-She shouldn't.

1103
01:55:59,726 --> 01:56:02,405
The less she walks around, the better it is.

1104
01:56:02,806 --> 01:56:04,125
Mother, but...

1105
01:56:05,206 --> 01:56:08,725
If she doesn't eat anything, she will fall weak.

1106
01:56:09,166 --> 01:56:11,485
I'll take food to her with your permission.

1107
01:56:16,006 --> 01:56:17,165
Do it.

1108
01:56:17,486 --> 01:56:19,085
But be careful, dear.

1109
01:56:19,726 --> 01:56:23,405
Although she protected
your life, she is our enemy.

1110
01:56:23,806 --> 01:56:25,125
Come on.

1111
01:56:29,966 --> 01:56:32,245
She is merciful like you.

1112
01:56:32,326 --> 01:56:35,645
God willing, this mercy will
not cause us trouble, Ulgen.

1113
01:56:35,646 --> 01:56:36,405
God willing.

1114
01:56:36,766 --> 01:56:39,925
I made delicious sherbet,
would you like to drink some?

1115
01:56:39,926 --> 01:56:41,645
Yes, I would.

1116
01:56:46,686 --> 01:56:49,285
You should hold your sword stronger.

1117
01:56:58,246 --> 01:57:01,885
Sisters, you continue. Come on.

1118
01:57:05,046 --> 01:57:07,645
What are you doing here, huh?

1119
01:57:09,926 --> 01:57:13,965
Don't you hear me? I am
talking to you, are you deaf?

1120
01:57:13,966 --> 01:57:15,765
Are you talking to me?

1121
01:57:16,126 --> 01:57:17,445
No.

1122
01:57:17,526 --> 01:57:19,845
I'm talking to the axe over there.

1123
01:57:19,886 --> 01:57:22,205
You both sound the same anyway!

1124
01:57:22,326 --> 01:57:25,005
You recognized me quickly, Kayi girl.

1125
01:57:27,206 --> 01:57:29,965
I am as strong as an axe.

1126
01:57:29,966 --> 01:57:32,485
I can defeat anyone I strike with my sword.

1127
01:57:32,686 --> 01:57:35,685
Who are you? Are you an Alp?

1128
01:57:35,686 --> 01:57:37,605
It's clear you're new.

1129
01:57:38,046 --> 01:57:41,125
If you're not afraid of being
defeated, practice with me.

1130
01:57:41,126 --> 01:57:45,325
But if you manage to drop my sword, Kayi girl...

1131
01:57:45,886 --> 01:57:48,045
..I'll tell you who I am.

1132
01:57:48,966 --> 01:57:52,045
I don't practice with everyone.

1133
01:57:52,326 --> 01:57:55,845
Especially not with a madman like you.

1134
01:57:58,126 --> 01:57:59,925
Go and leave me alone.

1135
01:58:00,126 --> 01:58:02,245
Or just tell me you are scared.

1136
01:58:06,886 --> 01:58:10,965
Give me patience, Allah!

1137
01:58:14,366 --> 01:58:16,965
Are you really crazy?

1138
01:58:17,086 --> 01:58:18,285
What are you saying?

1139
01:58:18,286 --> 01:58:22,645
Do you want to die? Don't you know who she is?

1140
01:58:22,646 --> 01:58:23,725
Who is she?

1141
01:58:23,726 --> 01:58:25,525
I feel sorry for you.

1142
01:58:25,806 --> 01:58:30,205
You were a good Alp. But your time is up.

1143
01:58:30,206 --> 01:58:36,245
The Hatun you just said was scared is
Osman Bey's daughter, Fatma Hatun.

1144
01:58:41,326 --> 01:58:43,485
Now, calculate what's going to happen.

1145
01:58:43,486 --> 01:58:48,285
Yes, calculate, but don't go over the limit!

1146
01:58:54,366 --> 01:58:57,245
Osman Bey's daughter Fatma Hatun?

1147
01:59:01,926 --> 01:59:04,525
What am I doing here?

1148
01:59:07,606 --> 01:59:10,245
Damn you, Claudius.

1149
01:59:11,966 --> 01:59:14,965
Because of you, I lost everything.

1150
01:59:20,566 --> 01:59:23,205
I said I am not going to eat your food.

1151
01:59:26,766 --> 01:59:29,845
Why don't you understand?

1152
01:59:35,886 --> 01:59:37,725
You haven't eaten anything.

1153
01:59:38,046 --> 01:59:41,285
You're sick. You need to eat.

1154
01:59:44,366 --> 01:59:45,965
Poena.

1155
01:59:47,766 --> 01:59:49,325
My little bird.

1156
01:59:52,366 --> 01:59:54,525
Do you care about me like before?

1157
01:59:54,526 --> 01:59:56,285
My name is Halime.

1158
01:59:59,166 --> 02:00:00,805
I just...

1159
02:00:01,486 --> 02:00:03,925
I don't want to owe you anything.

1160
02:00:09,486 --> 02:00:11,965
You don't owe me anything.

1161
02:00:12,246 --> 02:00:14,685
Look at our situation.

1162
02:00:14,686 --> 02:00:18,525
I lost you, I lost Bursa I have nothing left.

1163
02:00:26,206 --> 02:00:28,685
Look at this.

1164
02:00:32,966 --> 02:00:34,565
Poena.

1165
02:00:35,886 --> 02:00:39,045
I raised you for ten years.

1166
02:00:40,326 --> 02:00:42,005
My little bird.

1167
02:00:44,126 --> 02:00:46,485
This is not you.

1168
02:00:49,686 --> 02:00:51,965
You threw me into darkness.

1169
02:00:59,086 --> 02:01:01,405
I found peace with Islam.

1170
02:01:04,886 --> 02:01:06,805
This is me, Sofia.

1171
02:01:08,366 --> 02:01:10,045
I am Halime.

1172
02:01:11,166 --> 02:01:12,605
And I...

1173
02:01:13,406 --> 02:01:15,685
Thank Allah, I am Muslim.

1174
02:01:22,766 --> 02:01:24,885
Poena..

1175
02:01:30,206 --> 02:01:33,005
Damn it..

1176
02:01:34,806 --> 02:01:40,565
-Osman Bey welcome! 
-Thank you!

1177
02:01:42,366 --> 02:01:44,005
Thank you.

1178
02:01:45,646 --> 02:01:47,565
Thank you.

1179
02:01:49,246 --> 02:01:50,805
Thank you.

1180
02:02:08,046 --> 02:02:12,605
Welcome my Bey!

1181
02:02:12,606 --> 02:02:18,005
Thank you, thank you.

1182
02:02:18,806 --> 02:02:21,405
We heard the enemies lost and faced defeat.

1183
02:02:21,406 --> 02:02:24,285
May your victory be blessed, my Bey. Welcome.

1184
02:02:24,286 --> 02:02:26,525
Thank you, Bala. Thank you.

1185
02:02:26,526 --> 02:02:30,925
Make preparations. We will
celebrate this with a feast.

1186
02:02:30,926 --> 02:02:32,645
As you order.

1187
02:02:32,726 --> 02:02:37,325
Come on Hatuns. Prepare the meals. Set the fire.

1188
02:02:37,326 --> 02:02:39,805
Let's go. Sisters. Come on!

1189
02:02:48,606 --> 02:02:54,565
The enemies of Islam in the frontiers
have been punished by your sword, my Bey.

1190
02:02:54,566 --> 02:02:55,645
Thank you.

1191
02:02:55,646 --> 02:02:58,750
In the frontiers, you
kept the light of Islam eternal...

1192
02:02:58,762 --> 02:03:02,285
...and destroyed the
dogs of the devil, my Bey.

1193
02:03:02,286 --> 02:03:04,365
Thank you!

1194
02:03:04,366 --> 02:03:08,605
May Allah grant you a long life, my Bey.

1195
02:03:08,686 --> 02:03:11,605
May your state be everlasting.

1196
02:03:11,886 --> 02:03:13,365
Thank you

1197
02:03:13,366 --> 02:03:15,445
Thank you, live long.

1198
02:03:24,006 --> 02:03:25,845
Peace be upon you.

1199
02:03:25,926 --> 02:03:27,525
Peace be upon you too.

1200
02:03:30,326 --> 02:03:31,765
Where is Sofia, Bala?

1201
02:03:31,886 --> 02:03:33,485
She is in her tent, my Bey.

1202
02:03:33,486 --> 02:03:35,325
She hasn't come out all day.

1203
02:03:35,326 --> 02:03:37,285
I will talk to her.

1204
02:03:48,246 --> 02:03:50,365
Let's see what happens now...

1205
02:03:53,886 --> 02:03:55,525
-Yigit.
-Brother.

1206
02:03:55,526 --> 02:03:59,205
Set out immediately and
bring our people to the feast.

1207
02:03:59,206 --> 02:04:03,765
Bring them here, so that
they can witness our victory.

1208
02:04:05,006 --> 02:04:06,845
As you order, brother.

1209
02:04:07,126 --> 02:04:08,845
My brave son...

1210
02:04:09,486 --> 02:04:11,965
My brave Oguz son, like his name.

1211
02:04:17,846 --> 02:04:19,445
Osman Bey.

1212
02:04:20,726 --> 02:04:23,565
What is happening? No
one is telling me anything!

1213
02:04:25,726 --> 02:04:27,325
Kucar died.

1214
02:04:27,326 --> 02:04:29,725
His army is destroyed.

1215
02:04:29,886 --> 02:04:31,165
What?

1216
02:04:33,046 --> 02:04:34,325
How did that happen?

1217
02:04:34,326 --> 02:04:36,165
It was not difficult.

1218
02:04:36,446 --> 02:04:38,485
I made an agreement with Claudius.

1219
02:04:38,646 --> 02:04:41,805
And I destroyed Kucar's army.

1220
02:04:48,766 --> 02:04:50,325
How did you manage that?

1221
02:04:50,326 --> 02:04:55,685
With the gold of the
Emperor, I ruined their alliance.

1222
02:05:01,246 --> 02:05:02,805
Now..

1223
02:05:03,166 --> 02:05:04,805
...Claudius...

1224
02:05:05,526 --> 02:05:07,565
...is the only ruler of Bursa.

1225
02:05:08,806 --> 02:05:11,565
And he is the only enemy of the Emperor.

1226
02:05:18,966 --> 02:05:22,165
...you left the Emperor and
Claudius alone to face each other.

1227
02:05:23,046 --> 02:05:25,165
You divided Byzantium.

1228
02:05:30,686 --> 02:05:33,405
You really surprised me greatly, Osman Bey.

1229
02:05:33,406 --> 02:05:34,885
I mean...

1230
02:05:36,086 --> 02:05:37,725
...it's a smart plan.

1231
02:05:37,726 --> 02:05:39,005
What is it?

1232
02:05:39,446 --> 02:05:42,445
Are you the only one who
knows how to play games, huh?

1233
02:05:43,846 --> 02:05:46,605
Of course we know how to play games.

1234
02:05:46,606 --> 02:05:48,285
But you..

1235
02:05:48,566 --> 02:05:54,445
...not only like playing games against
your enemies, but also against each other.

1236
02:06:00,326 --> 02:06:03,605
Now you don't have an army in Bursa.

1237
02:06:05,326 --> 02:06:07,205
What will you do now?

1238
02:06:10,166 --> 02:06:14,725
What will you do now?

1239
02:06:19,126 --> 02:06:22,005
By making an agreement with my enemy Claudius...

1240
02:06:28,606 --> 02:06:31,405
...you betrayed me, Osman Bey!

1241
02:06:31,406 --> 02:06:33,965
Your own people betrayed you.

1242
02:06:34,326 --> 02:06:36,125
You are still in my tribe.

1243
02:06:36,126 --> 02:06:37,925
You are still alive.

1244
02:06:39,726 --> 02:06:41,805
I am loyal to our agreement.

1245
02:06:43,846 --> 02:06:46,165
You killed Kucar.

1246
02:06:47,046 --> 02:06:48,765
You won.

1247
02:06:49,806 --> 02:06:51,085
What about me?

1248
02:06:51,606 --> 02:06:53,765
Me, Osman Bey...

1249
02:06:53,766 --> 02:06:55,325
I lost Bursa!

1250
02:06:55,326 --> 02:06:57,125
What was going to happen?!

1251
02:06:57,446 --> 02:07:00,325
Was I supposed to give Bursa
to you on a golden platter?

1252
02:07:00,966 --> 02:07:02,565
Look at me!

1253
02:07:03,726 --> 02:07:05,885
You protected my daughter.

1254
02:07:05,966 --> 02:07:07,565
Therefore...

1255
02:07:08,326 --> 02:07:11,565
You will stay here as a
guest for a while longer.

1256
02:07:18,046 --> 02:07:20,285
You no longer...

1257
02:07:21,206 --> 02:07:23,085
...have a state...

1258
02:07:24,166 --> 02:07:26,485
...or an army that will fight for you.

1259
02:07:28,486 --> 02:07:30,685
Now go and build yourself a new life.

1260
02:07:38,726 --> 02:07:40,565
Come on sisters! Come on!

1261
02:07:40,566 --> 02:07:44,245
It will get dark soon.
Come on, there's a lot to do.

1262
02:07:45,926 --> 02:07:46,605
Kismet!

1263
02:07:46,766 --> 02:07:49,725
You are quite fast while fighting, sister.

1264
02:07:49,926 --> 02:07:53,485
Come on! Come on! Everyone hurry up!

1265
02:07:54,126 --> 02:07:55,085
Let me see that..

1266
02:07:55,086 --> 02:07:58,925
Don't run away!

1267
02:07:58,926 --> 02:07:59,725
What is this?

1268
02:07:59,806 --> 02:08:01,485
Put some more molasses in this.

1269
02:08:01,486 --> 02:08:04,005
Put another jug of molasses in it. Ghazi!

1270
02:08:04,606 --> 02:08:06,005
Don't wander around!

1271
02:08:06,086 --> 02:08:07,525
I am playing a game, mother!

1272
02:08:07,526 --> 02:08:09,485
Do you have to play right here, my son?

1273
02:08:09,486 --> 02:08:11,925
Let them play, Ulgen. Let them.

1274
02:08:11,926 --> 02:08:13,685
Ghazi, take it, my son.

1275
02:08:14,206 --> 02:08:16,645
Thank you Bala Hatun.

1276
02:08:17,686 --> 02:08:19,365
Look at him..

1277
02:08:21,246 --> 02:08:22,965
May it be easy Hatuns.

1278
02:08:22,966 --> 02:08:24,645
Thank you.

1279
02:08:24,646 --> 02:08:26,365
Let me see the keshkek meal.

1280
02:08:26,366 --> 02:08:27,885
Let me check.

1281
02:08:35,086 --> 02:08:38,645
Keshkek will be done soon.

1282
02:08:39,086 --> 02:08:42,845
Ulgen, make the fire stronger.

1283
02:08:42,846 --> 02:08:44,405
Right away, my Bala.

1284
02:08:44,966 --> 02:08:46,525
Here, sister.

1285
02:08:46,886 --> 02:08:48,005
Is it good?

1286
02:08:48,006 --> 02:08:51,645
We've cooked the halva, after adding
some more molasses it'll be ready.

1287
02:08:51,646 --> 02:08:53,285
Thanks to your hands.

1288
02:08:53,366 --> 02:08:54,045
Thank you.

1289
02:08:54,046 --> 02:08:57,205
Add plenty, we must have more than we
need or it won't be enough for everyone.

1290
02:08:57,206 --> 02:08:59,525
Give everyone plenty of these meals.

1291
02:08:59,526 --> 02:09:03,045
On this blessed day, let's
make sure we all enjoy the meals.

1292
02:09:03,966 --> 02:09:04,805
Good.

1293
02:09:04,806 --> 02:09:07,405
Make sure everything is complete. Come on!

1294
02:09:07,406 --> 02:09:09,205
Come on sisters!

1295
02:09:09,766 --> 02:09:12,445
Good, good, sister. Praise be.

1296
02:09:32,086 --> 02:09:33,885
No troubles happened, Bala Hatun.

1297
02:09:40,046 --> 02:09:43,645
I carried out my duty, Bala Hatun.

1298
02:09:45,286 --> 02:09:47,725
What will you do to me now?

1299
02:09:48,406 --> 02:09:49,805
Kill me?

1300
02:09:52,126 --> 02:09:54,365
Your soul is so evil..

1301
02:09:56,206 --> 02:09:59,325
...that you don't believe we
will keep our promise, do you?

1302
02:09:59,526 --> 02:10:01,525
You think we will act like you.

1303
02:10:01,686 --> 02:10:05,245
-I am...
You're the victim of your ambitions, Begum.

1304
02:10:06,206 --> 02:10:08,445
You wanted to take what wasn't yours.

1305
02:10:10,326 --> 02:10:13,085
Your eyes, soul and heart were blind.

1306
02:10:15,166 --> 02:10:19,365
You spoke of death, but no.
Death isn't your punishment.

1307
02:10:20,406 --> 02:10:22,525
Your biggest punishment is...

1308
02:10:22,646 --> 02:10:27,645
...drifting away without roots
and traditions like a withered leaf.

1309
02:10:29,446 --> 02:10:31,485
Now get out of my tribe.

1310
02:10:31,686 --> 02:10:33,845
And never come back.

1311
02:10:34,046 --> 02:10:35,525
Get out of my sight!

1312
02:10:37,006 --> 02:10:38,325
Get out!

1313
02:11:09,086 --> 02:11:10,325
Stop!

1314
02:11:14,326 --> 02:11:18,045
Commander Claudius wants to see you.

1315
02:11:18,966 --> 02:11:21,685
I have nothing to do with Byzantine heathens.

1316
02:11:23,246 --> 02:11:25,525
You had things to do with Kucar, though!

1317
02:11:28,046 --> 02:11:30,925
Do you think I don't know you were serving him?

1318
02:11:31,326 --> 02:11:32,605
Me?

1319
02:11:33,166 --> 02:11:34,405
Yes, you.

1320
02:11:39,566 --> 02:11:43,645
I'll offer you two options.

1321
02:11:45,046 --> 02:11:48,765
To be able to survive you will serve me.

1322
02:11:49,446 --> 02:11:53,965
Or I will go tell Osman about
how you served Kucar like a dog.

1323
02:11:56,406 --> 02:12:00,365
Whichever you prefer.

1324
02:12:01,726 --> 02:12:02,765
Your choice.

1325
02:12:30,766 --> 02:12:33,085
